{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5","id":1227922,"title":"M5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-16T18:20:02-07:00","id":1227922,"title":"M5","content":"Excited for M5? Why not go and list changes you want to see while you wait? Let's come up with ideas for the new edition together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T20:31:35-07:00","id":1227946,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I can properly contextualize all the changes I would like to make to the mechanics, though most would be tweaks rather than full blown rule changes. So instead of that I will talk about major setting differences I would make.<br /> <br /> First off I would build upon the Technocracy being on the brink of a civil war, not just between Conventions but also between different groups inside Conventions (particularly in the case of the Syndicate and NWO). I'd also like to have there control over technological development get out from under them with them no longer being able to control how 'mundane' technology progresses like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions\">this</a> has been talking about.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Traditions I would have them for the most part have learned their lessons that caused their internal strife. I would keep the issues definitely but better able to work together. That said, their effectiveness would still be limited on the whole as recovering from all the damage they went through would still take time so most of the Traditions would be more focused on recruitment and rebuilding. Not just that though, the Ascension War would also take a back seat to actually learning, following their paradigm, and actually trying to reach Ascension.<br /> <br /> Then there is the Crafts. I would put more focus on them as well. The game would still focus primarily on the Traditions but it would be very clear that the 9 Traditions aren't the end all be all of magical though. For example, just because the Dreamspeakers are typically animistic that doesn't mean every onmyouji would be a part of them. Revised attempts to cut Crafts and make them all a part of a Tradition was always something annoying to me.<br /> <br /> I like mystic threads and reality zones and I would also very much expand on them as well<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T00:13:34-07:00","id":1227978,"title":"","content":"For the game mechanics, I'd like more clarity in the rules. Not even real changes, just a lot better explanations. As it is now, there are so many words left unexplained that a new player or storyteller doesn't know what's actually happening ingame. I feel Mage is very prone to house rules and different interpretations of the existing rules due to this. I actually don't want a V5, just a bit more streamlining and way more supplements.<br /> <br /> The big part is the metaplot. Don't know where it should go, but I think the Crafts need more love. M20 did a good job listing most of them but we need a few more books on them.<br /> I also feel like the non american continents need a bit more depths. Maybe a few adventures to highlight the differences to America.<br /> <br /> We don't know how M5 will be, but there is a good chance that I might stay with M20 rules and just take the metaplot. Or maybe I'll make up the further metaplot on my own. I really can't tell at this point, as I don't know how much retconning there will be.<br /> But nonetheless I will be interested in how M5 works out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T14:32:40-07:00","id":1228118,"title":"","content":"Biggest changes I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> 1. Level One Sphere abilities could use a boost. Time and Matter especially.<br /> 2. People have pointed this out, but with AI development growing exponentially it feels weird that you need Mind 5 to create a self-aware AI.<br /> 3. Overhaul the Technocracy. They were great antagonists in the 90s but the times have changed and while I know they aren't really supposed to be represent the evils of technology, the stigma is still there regardless of intention. I'd would love it if the Traditions vs Technocracy Ascension War was left as a relic of the past. Take the Kinder, Softer Technocracy approach and leave the 1984 mind control and &quot;Let's sent terminators to murder pagans and theoretical scientists we don't like&quot; baggage behind. The Trads and Technocracy don't have to be friends but they don't have to be assumed to be enemies either. Threat Null, Marauders, Nephandi and weird supernatural WTFuckery can the main antagonists of the setting.<br /> 4. Update the Hollow Ones. I don't know how, but the Goth thing has run its course, I think.<br /> 5. Reduce Skill blot. Seriously, even as a secondary skill having Jetpack in M20 was ridiculous.<br /> 6. Play up the diversity of the Traditions. There's no reason why the Celestial Chorus, Verbena, and Order of Hermes need to be assumed to overwhelming white in the modern day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 06-17-2018, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T15:32:00-07:00","id":1228132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1228118#post1228118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biggest changes I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> 1. Level One Sphere abilities could use a boost. Time and Matter especially.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make a changes to a number of Spheres but yeah, making Time more useful or at least explaining how to make Time 1 more useful would be up there<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. People have pointed this out, but with AI development growing exponentially it feels weird that you need Mind 5 to create a self-aware AI. </div> </div> </div>One of the changes I would do is make certain Spheres more progressive in some areas. Mind for example, Level 5 would be necessary to truly aware and sapient AI and other artificial minds. But I would allow Level 4 to make sentient minds, kind of like animal minds or something lacking a full consciousness and is limited by the function it was designed for. Mind 3 would allow 'simple' creations that are able to follow instructions or have limited reasoning ability. I think this would better represent the flow of AI technology into the Consensus but still have the Enlightened AI creations still be better than what is currently available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Overhaul the Technocracy. They were great antagonists in the 90s but the times have changed and while I know they aren't really supposed to be represent the evils of technology, the stigma is still there regardless of intention. I'd would love it if the Traditions vs Technocracy Ascension War was left as a relic of the past. Take the Kinder, Softer Technocracy approach and leave the 1984 mind control and &quot;Let's sent terminators to murder pagans and theoretical scientists we don't like&quot; baggage behind. The Trads and Technocracy don't have to be friends but they don't have to be assumed to be enemies either. Threat Null, Marauders, Nephandi and weird supernatural WTFuckery can the main antagonists of the setting. </div> </div> </div>I have mixed feelings about this. While I think the Ascension War should be more of a background element I don't think it should removed. Arguably it's more relevant now in today's world than it was back 20 years ago. What with the rise of pseudoscience, political environment, religious issues, corporate influence, and so on. I'd like a lot of this to be something that has gotten out of hand and both the Traditions and Technocracy no longer have much control over it. Whether that is because of Nephandi or Threat Null influence or just the consequences of human nature I would leave a bit ambiguous. But I would like the Technocracy to stop being the go to cliche bad guys. I would like there to still be strife between them and the Traditions over how to fix the world and each groups' methods conflict with their own but not have the old &quot;Reality Deviants must be destroyed!&quot; methods they used to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Update the Hollow Ones. I don't know how, but the Goth thing has run its course, I think. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I'd have them expanded to all kinds of counter culture ideals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Reduce Skill blot. Seriously, even a secondary skill having Jetpack in M20 was ridiculous. </div> </div> </div>Very much agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. Play up the diversity of the Traditions. There's no reason why the Celestial Chorus, Verbena, and Order of Hermes need to be assumed to overwhelming white in the modern day. </div> </div> </div>This I like, I would also go into the diversity of belief as well. Example with showing other lines of Verbana paganism beyond the witch look it's primarily had, like Ancient Greek Paganism or Mesoamerican Paganism. I've always found the Dead Magic books to be good for expanding Verbana character ideas. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T23:08:23-07:00","id":1228212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1228118#post1228118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. People have pointed this out, but with AI development growing exponentially it feels weird that you need Mind 5 to create a self-aware AI.</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly disagree. Just because &quot;AI&quot; is being tossed around as a marketing gimmick term a lot lately for Deep-Learning systems does not mean that Mind 5 suddenly isn't required anymore to create a full-fledged, self-aware concience.<br /> <br /> Or put in other words, we still don't understand how the brain actually works. We still don't understand how thought processes exactly happen, or even how to define intelligent sentience or how self-awareness works. The brain literally remains the most complex object we know of in the entire universe.<br /> And the most complex neural setup we have accurately reproduced on par with nature so far is that of the roundworm - which has 302 neurons. For reference, an ant has 250000 neurons.<br /> I can't stress enough that todays &quot;Artificial Intelligence&quot; as used in marketing has absolutely nothing to do with anything resembling thought or conscious intelligence.<br /> And with &quot;AI&quot; being used for anything that uses external sensors and learning algorithms these days, we really ought to start differentiating between &quot;Artificial Intelligence&quot; and &quot;Artificial Sentience/Concience&quot;, because when it comes to the latter we've still not gotten anywhere at all.<br /> <br /> Now, what *is* happening however is that, thanks to &quot;AI&quot; Assistants everywhere, a Mage who gets sleeper visitors these days can pull off the existance of their talking digital buddy as something coincidental more and more.<br /> <br /> Mage. &quot;Ah. Artemis? We are getting vistors, so, could you..um. You know?&quot;<br /> Artemis: &quot;Play dumb again? Really Doctor? You know how uncomfortable that makes me.&quot;<br /> Mage: *sighs* &quot;I know Artemis, I know. Someday, but for now..please?&quot;<br /> Artemis: &quot;I know Doctor. It is just frustrating.&quot;<br /> Mage: &quot;..please do not Rickroll us again when I ask you to shuffle my playlist?&quot;<br /> Artemis: &quot;I will promise nothing of the sort.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> On that note, I *do* agree that simpler minds like those of non-primate animals should maybe require only Mind 4. There have been rotes in the old books where a Mage creates that kind of animal companion without Mind at all, but that does a disservice to those creatures, as many many animals out there are far beyond being steered by only instinct. Especially the kind of animals we keep as companions. It should be a stacked tier of Mind 3-5 depending on the degree of complexity,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-18-2018, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T04:11:57-07:00","id":1228249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1228132#post1228132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have mixed feelings about this. While I think the Ascension War should be more of a background element I don't think it should removed. Arguably it's more relevant now in today's world than it was back 20 years ago. What with the rise of pseudoscience, political environment, religious issues, corporate influence, and so on. I'd like a lot of this to be something that has gotten out of hand and both the Traditions and Technocracy no longer have much control over it. Whether that is because of Nephandi or Threat Null influence or just the consequences of human nature I would leave a bit ambiguous. But I would like the Technocracy to stop being the go to cliche bad guys. I would like there to still be strife between them and the Traditions over how to fix the world and each groups' methods conflict with their own but not have the old &quot;Reality Deviants must be destroyed!&quot; methods they used to have.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do think the 'teams' could change as far as the Ascencion War goes. More reflective of the current climate rather than the 'we must have Sphere X' represented'.<br /> <br /> Where Science is no longer an enemy of Paganism or pleasure, but Banking, the Church, and Politics might be the 'strong arm' now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T07:19:07-07:00","id":1228284,"title":"","content":"Clear unique uses for every sphere at every level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T12:54:16-07:00","id":1228356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1228118#post1228118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biggest changes I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> 1. Level One Sphere abilities could use a boost. Time and Matter especially.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Choristers, screw your extra Quintessence! I don't need a watch, how 'bout that!&quot; - Unidentified Ecstacist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T15:22:59-07:00","id":1228392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1228356#post1228356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Choristers, screw your extra Quintessence! I don't need a watch, how 'bout that!&quot; - Unidentified Ecstacist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I let it buff things that require perfect timing, dancing, music.. shooting people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T09:25:56-07:00","id":1228875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1228132#post1228132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd make a changes to a number of Spheres but yeah, making Time more useful or at least explaining how to make Time 1 more useful would be up there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main change I\u2019d make to the spheres would be to remove Prime (give the fuel/rip pattern parts to the respective spheres, the rest to spirit) and then split Entropy into Fate and Death and finally give sphere-specific summoning/realm travel to each of the spheres (and at a higher rank than Spirit can do it).<br /> <br /> Basically try to make the need for conjunctional magic a bit less necessary and thus which spheres are needed for various effects more intuitive.<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019d then also add a second specialty sphere and an inferior sphere based on your avatar essence; Dymanic (mind or spirit), Pattern (forces, matter or life), Questing (space or time) and Primordial (fate or death) with the inferior sphere being one from the next essence in the cycle (the idea being that what\u2019s hardest for your avatar is the next step... if your avatar is questing, then you\u2019ll have a harder time with magic related to the end of the journey. If your avatar is primordial then endings are easy, but new beginnings (ideas conceived by Mind and given form in Spirit) are hard. The same for going from new ideas to putting them into practice and from building something to then really exploring what\u2019s been built (instead of building the next thing... which is easy for the pattern essence).<br /> <br /> This would then supplement the specialty spheres of the Traditions/Conventions so that anyone regardless of tradition could be a specialist in any given sphere. That said, I think I\u2019d establish a \u201cchoice of two\u201d approach to the Tradition specialty spheres as a default instead of optional variants (ex. Forces and Spirit for the Order of Hermes since summoning and spirit pacts are just as much part of the Order\u2019s practices as manipulating fundamental forces is)... either that or kill the notion that tradition has anything to do with specialty spheres at all (i.e. Tradition determines your Focus, not what sphere you have the easiest time using).<br /> <br /> I think there are a number of things that could be done to help mechanically support the fluff aspects of the magic system and make it more intuitive for newer players. The M20 revisions to Focus (paradigm, practice, props) were definitely a step in the right direction and making your Essence matter and the spheres be more intuitive in their conjunctions (ex. Taking the Death sphere if you want to be a necromancy type is intuitive... needing matter, prime, spirit and just a bit of entropy; which also allows dozens of other unrelated magics; is not intuitive at all).<br /> <br /> At least that would be the approach I\u2019d take to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T11:07:13-07:00","id":1228909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1228875#post1228875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main change I\u2019d make to the spheres would be to remove Prime (give the fuel/rip pattern parts to the respective spheres, the rest to spirit) and then split Entropy into Fate and Death and finally give sphere-specific summoning/realm travel to each of the spheres (and at a higher rank than Spirit can do it).<br /> <br /> Basically try to make the need for conjunctional magic a bit less necessary and thus which spheres are needed for various effects more intuitive.<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019d then also add a second specialty sphere and an inferior sphere based on your avatar essence; Dymanic (mind or spirit), Pattern (forces, matter or life), Questing (space or time) and Primordial (fate or death) with the inferior sphere being one from the next essence in the cycle (the idea being that what\u2019s hardest for your avatar is the next step... if your avatar is questing, then you\u2019ll have a harder time with magic related to the end of the journey. If your avatar is primordial then endings are easy, but new beginnings (ideas conceived by Mind and given form in Spirit) are hard. The same for going from new ideas to putting them into practice and from building something to then really exploring what\u2019s been built (instead of building the next thing... which is easy for the pattern essence).<br /> <br /> This would then supplement the specialty spheres of the Traditions/Conventions so that anyone regardless of tradition could be a specialist in any given sphere. That said, I think I\u2019d establish a \u201cchoice of two\u201d approach to the Tradition specialty spheres as a default instead of optional variants (ex. Forces and Spirit for the Order of Hermes since summoning and spirit pacts are just as much part of the Order\u2019s practices as manipulating fundamental forces is)... either that or kill the notion that tradition has anything to do with specialty spheres at all (i.e. Tradition determines your Focus, not what sphere you have the easiest time using).<br /> <br /> I think there are a number of things that could be done to help mechanically support the fluff aspects of the magic system and make it more intuitive for newer players. The M20 revisions to Focus (paradigm, practice, props) were definitely a step in the right direction and making your Essence matter and the spheres be more intuitive in their conjunctions (ex. Taking the Death sphere if you want to be a necromancy type is intuitive... needing matter, prime, spirit and just a bit of entropy; which also allows dozens of other unrelated magics; is not intuitive at all).<br /> <br /> At least that would be the approach I\u2019d take to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to be that guy.. but it sounds like you want to make Awakening<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T16:36:15-07:00","id":1229007,"title":"","content":"Nah, Awakening\u2019s fluff wouldn\u2019t amount to a single Tradition in terms of depth (and a Tradition I\u2019d never play at that because I loathe its paradigm) and, mechanically speaking variable difficulties with mostly static dice pools works a lot better with the magic system (frankly static difficulty and counting successes may as well just use a d20 with margins of success).<br /> <br /> That said, there are some useful mechanical widgets in Awakening that are useful and making the magic system more intuitive doesn\u2019t seem like a bad thing to me.<br /> <br /> Ascension\u2019s system of magic is great, but its particular breakdown of spheres is not the most intuitive for new players. It\u2019s quite possible for a new player to try to build for a theme and then end up completely unable to do that theme because they didn\u2019t get what Prime is for (so the guy who wants to throw fireballs actually can\u2019t) or other less intuitive conjunctions; I use \u201canimate dead\u201d because its an excellent example of a non-intuitive set of spheres for an effect (matter and prime; which also covers creating matter from nothing).<br /> <br /> Similarly, the shamanic paradigms being essentially worthless without conjunctional spirit (depending on interpretations of process-based determinism) is another non-intuitive aspect.<br /> <br /> Dropping Prime as a distinct sphere is because it is easily the least intuitive of the spheres for new players (at least in my two decades of experience introducing new players to the system).<br /> <br /> Similarly, the reason I specifically think splitting off Death from Entropy makes valid sense is because it fits the WoD cosmology... Mind allows access to the high umbra/Astral reaches, the middle umbra is most associated with the spirit sphere proper due to it being the primary sphere of the dreamspeakers, but to access the low umbra you need... conjunctional spirit and entropy (which also creates a false equivalence between the entropy sphere and death magic). Adding a death sphere makes the connections a bit more overt and intuitive (and also makes conjunctional magic to affect vampires and wraiths a bit more in line with being able to use straight spirit versus middle umbra entities and conjunctional spirit to affect werewolves).<br /> <br /> Maybe you don\u2019t interact much with new players, but I\u2019ve had to teach the system to a minimum of two new players a year for more than a decade now and the system is needlessly opaque for anyone trying to get into the game on their own.<br /> <br /> The M20 Focus rules were a great start in terms of making the concept of paradigm and foci from previous editions easier for new players to wrap their brains around and \u201croll your Arete and count successes regardless of spheres known\u201d is far superior for new players to Awakening\u2019s roll of most appropriate sphere + \u201cappropriate\u201d attribute + \u201cappropriate\u201d skill (it basically creates the need for a<br /> \u2018Spell List\u201d to keep track of each rote\u2019s dice pool) for rote based spells and Gnosis + most appropriate sphere for non-rotes.<br /> <br /> But you could add to that by actually making your Avatar Essence actually matter for your casting in more than just a fluff sense. It creates roleplaying hooks in the sense of where your character excels and what aspects will be a bigger challenge to them (heck, I could even see pursuing the more difficult spheres for your Essence type as part of the prerequisite for advancing your Arete past certain levels; you\u2019ll never move beyond say, Arete 5, if you don\u2019t actually push your boundaries... as an example). My experience is that the more something matters mechanically, the more the players will pay attention to it.<br /> <br /> As to why the spheres might change... the very setting includes the fact that they\u2019re somewhat arbitrary to begin with (hence the pillars of Pre-Tradition Coucil paradigms); so why not make them more intuitive?<br /> <br /> At least that\u2019s my opinion on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 06-20-2018, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T02:32:45-07:00","id":1229119,"title":"","content":"-Remove unnecessary complications from HDYDT book. Like requiring matter+space to set-up spirit ward. also remove automatic countermagic from other splats with Occult dice. <br /> -add an alternative of Gene-modded Organisms progenitor merit for appropriate traditions, like Verbana. <br /> -Introduce some more variety besides US mainland. I find there is very little fluf on mages in other continents/countries. <br /> -Would also like more description of some umbral realms and beings for mages. Including their involvement with mundane world.<br /> -Stop depicting mages either as GG or naphandi/infernalists. Define naphandi properly, it's not that hard damn it.<br /> -Better balanced Wonders. Some of them are either ridiculously overpriced or stupidly convoluted.<br /> -what do people think of Legacies in Ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T06:25:11-07:00","id":1229135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1229119#post1229119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-what do people think of Legacies in Ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the concept - the search for enlightenment forges your own soul, altering the way magick works - but the execution needs to be adjusted to Ascension's philosophy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T06:40:28-07:00","id":1229139,"title":"","content":"So, I thought that instead of giving lists of spirits and personae there should be a description of locale and the actors on it (including institutions, supernaturals and umbral ecology). Much like city books in CoD, but shorter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1229135#post1229135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the concept - the search for enlightenment forges your own soul, altering the way magick works - but the execution needs to be adjusted to Ascension's philosophy</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be tradition specific, not available for other paradigms or orphans. It should be very paradigm specific and preferably non-vulgar, probably bar the last attainment. For example:<br /> <br /> 1st Attainment - Arete 2, Sphere 2, Trait 3, Ability 3<br /> -Extraordinary perception, arete based buff to one trait or one covert modification<br /> 2nd Attainment - Arete 3, Sphere 2, Trait 4, Ability 4<br /> -Defense, mobile buff to traits, one borderline modification<br /> 3rd Attainment - Arete 4, Sphere 4, Trait 5, Ability 5<br /> -One vulgar magic for a scene, spend minimum 1wp, 1 Q and <i>maybe (?) </i>earn 1 (only 1) paradox if observed by sleepers.<br /> <br /> Quintecscence gathering rituals should also be somehow limited. Maybe spend 1 WP, roll Arete at 10-Sphere difficulty (minimum 5) and gain successes as Q points.<br /> <br /> Some subtler Legacies can be converted with very little problem, in particular those that deal with umbra or mental powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 06-21-2018, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T07:52:47-07:00","id":1229153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1229139#post1229139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it should be tradition specific, not available for other paradigms or orphans. It should be very paradigm specific and preferably non-vulgar, probably bar the last attainment. For example:<br /> <br /> 1st Attainment - Arete 2, Sphere 2, Trait 3, Ability 3<br /> -Extraordinary perception, arete based buff to one trait or one covert modification<br /> 2nd Attainment - Arete 3, Sphere 2, Trait 4, Ability 4<br /> -Defense, mobile buff to traits, one borderline modification<br /> 3rd Attainment - Arete 4, Sphere 4, Trait 5, Ability 5<br /> -One vulgar magic for a scene, spend minimum 1wp, 1 Q and <i>maybe (?) </i>earn 1 (only 1) paradox if observed by sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the first two, but I don't recomend anything that would alter the effects of Paradox. That doesn't jive well with Ascension's definition of Paradox (which it's not a personal relationship with the universe but relative to the area and beliefs), nor with the goals of the Ascencion War (the enlightenment to be able to cast without Paradox it's unimpressive in a Reality Zone that eliminates the problem) I would rather have Attainment's modify mechanical aspects magick that are unrelated to the whole Consensus thing and yet are the same for everyone disregarding the differences that Paradigm/Practice would suggest<br /> <br /> For instance: Heavy Arms had, in a previous post, suggested to eliminate the arbitrary bonus to damage that you get by using Forces, and instead get it as an Attainment (Say, Arete 3 Hermetics get 1 extra success to damage spells that use Forces). I like that idea.<br /> <br /> The Extatic bonus that allows to have one extra magical perception actived without penalties could be made an Attainment too.<br /> <br /> DO, instead of being a &quot;super skill&quot;, could be weaved as potent bonuses to Martial Arts granted trough Attainments - which incidentally would reinforce the Akashick belief in that their martial arts and their magick are one and the same.<br /> <br /> Similar advatages would be easy to fashion and would allow to ilustrate the advantages of different Traditions without entering into issues with the meaning of Paradox.<br /> <br /> The only &quot;spell-like habilities&quot; that I would recomend as an Attainment under these rules would be those that alter how magick works without involving Vulgarity at all.<br /> <br /> For instance, an Etherite (or a Verditus) could get the Prime effects that allow to create magical items trough Attainments, in order to eliminate the eternal problem of having to get Prime to create their fabled aparathuses, regardless of your disinterest in manipulating the stuff of magick itself. Note that the effect itself it's never Vulgar nor Coincident, because it's vulgarity depends on the effects weaved into the object.<br /> <br /> In the same fashion, I would take the Prime 1 &quot;advantage&quot; of being able to absorb Quintessence beyond your Avatar limits (which was never depicted as a spell, but rather as something you just &quot;can do&quot; when you get Prime 1) and fashion it as an Attaiment. Same with Spirit &quot;Extra Soak against Spirits&quot;. <hr /><br /> While Traditions should have specific Attainments (and have special options corresponding to their camps. I.E: so a Bonisagus could get different Attainments than a Flambeau), I think that some other groups should get them too.<br /> <br /> Crafts value their special practices even more than the Traditions, as many refused to join to preserve their own paths to enlightenment. Attainments to make them really different from the Traditions and each other would be very cool and would reinforce the idea that their stile of magick it's different. If anything, I would make more restrictive Attainments for them (perhaps heavily empowering one type of magick or action while weakening other types)<br /> <br /> Technocrats supposedly have a &quot;Unified Paradigm&quot;, but they're very serious about enlightenment and there's no reason to believe they wouldn't be changed by it: Eventually a Technocrat does become Control. They should get a single set of Attainments regardless of Convention...except that all Conventions have their own views about enlightenment. An ItX that desires to follow the cult of the machine should have that choice reflected in his soul. These alternate paths to enlightenment shouldn't be cherished, as they're unmutual, but they should exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-21-2018, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T11:39:04-07:00","id":1229187,"title":"","content":"I don't see the problem. think you are overcomplicating.<br /> 3rd level attainment would cost 1 point of willpower and 1 point of quintessence to activate and earn a point of Paradox each scene (or use depending what it is). Of course it will be still rationalized away as normal. So I see it as more of a trump card in right spot then some sort of a game shattering power. Overusing it will still harm you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T13:36:40-07:00","id":1229216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1229187#post1229187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the problem. think you are overcomplicating.<br /> 3rd level attainment would cost 1 point of willpower and 1 point of quintessence to activate and earn a point of Paradox each scene (or use depending what it is). Of course it will be still rationalized away as normal. So I see it as more of a trump card in right spot then some sort of a game shattering power. Overusing it will still harm you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I was talking about had nothing to do with mechanical stuff. I never said it was OP - far from that: From a mechanical standpoint, remember that in M20 1 point of Paradox per Vulgar spell it's the norm (you will only get more in a botch). So your rule it's useful only when there's no witnesses. Not bad, but hardly a &quot;trump card&quot;.<br /> <br /> The real problem I see with that Attainment it's that it mingles poorly with delicate concepts that are core to the game.<br /> <br /> The idea that you can mess with paradox by being too entrenched in your own Tradition goes against the concept of Paradox as a reaction: In Mage the world rewards you for playing along (by &quot;fooling&quot; reality into believing that your're not doing magick) and punishes you for being too entrenched in your Tradition to adapt your magicks (by using impressive baddass legendary powers). In Mage old mages that are the exemplars of their Traditions, the best of the best, and can't conceive to adapt their power to the modern world get sealed in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> If anything, Attainments should give you MORE Paradox, because you're using your belief to, as you say, push a trump card - That's more power to your beliefs, power that it's pushing against reality even harder - and as the saying goes, for each action a reaction: Paradox it's Reality pushing back with conmesurate force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T00:04:29-07:00","id":1229315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1229216#post1229216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that you can mess with paradox by being too entrenched in your own Tradition goes against the concept of Paradox as a reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marauders. You are forgetting that you can play as marauder with quiet 1-3 and be nearly lucid, paradox-immune mage. Or put a few points into empty pariapt for sizable paradox battery.<br /> <br /> So again I do not see the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 06-22-2018, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T09:00:54-07:00","id":1229376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1229315#post1229315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Marauders. You are forgetting that you can play as marauder with quiet 1-3 and be nearly lucid, paradox-immune mage. Or put a few points into empty pariapt for sizable paradox battery.<br /> <br /> So again I do not see the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marauders soak Paradox but they're also soaked with it: They have Permanent Quiet. Quiet it's a form of Paradox. Hence, they do suffer Paradox, it's just that they suffer it in a different fashion.<br /> <br /> It's known that many Marauders start their careers as consequence of a potent Backlash or a disociation with Reality caused by long exposures to the Deep Umbra. Marauders it's what happens when mages say &quot;fuck Reality, I want none of that&quot;, and when that happens the consequences aren't nice: they aren't labeled as &quot;kill on sight&quot; by every faction for shit and giggles...And thus they're an integral part of the &quot;magick has consequences/reality pushes back&quot; theme of Mage<br /> <br /> Even storing Paradox into Periapts (which it's an exploit) doesn't eliminate the risk of Paradox: You always have the damocles sword of the Periapt exploding if you Botch while using them (they don't prevent Backlash, they just act as a bigger &quot;Paradox wheel&quot; that you can take off). <hr /><br /> So, again, it's a matter not of mechanics but of <b>theme</b>: Paradox it's the consequence of Hubris. I find weird that Attainments, of all things, work against Hubris - I would think that the opposite would be true as you're working upon your soul to improve it. It's a consequence of following your own reality-warping credo. If you can sell to me <i>a</i> <i>narrative </i>(rather than referencing mechanical exploits) that explains how Attainments decrease the friction between Reality and your magick, I would accept it.<br /> <br /> Even then, it could be improved by adding some sort of &quot;damocles sword&quot; clause: Familiars can explode, Prime 5 can Botch, the Umbra makes you crazy, what kind of Paradox related risk does this Attainment involve?. Expending resources it's nice for game balance and all, but it's not enough to make it <b><i>thematic</i></b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T14:24:31-07:00","id":1229649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1228118#post1228118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Level One Sphere abilities could use a boost. Time and Matter especially.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think that Matter 1 should be improved / made better ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T00:04:21-07:00","id":1231309,"title":"","content":"Some backgrounds need to change.<br /> -Totems should be available for other mages too, though in different forms. Hermetics would have spirit guide with no problem, choristers a guardian angel, etc.<br /> -Pheromone Glands should be renamed, humans don't use pheromone manipulation and lack senses to detect them effectively. Something like Retrovirus Pods would be more appropriate.<br /> -Additional petty abilities (like stone lore or jetpack flight) should be removed, either moved to merits or just ability specialties. they just clutter up the space.<br /> -For the love of god, change illustration style. most of it either looks like a cartoon or rips off CoD in terrible way. Too much gloss and too much old tarot cards everywhere.<br /> -Again on naphandi. right now every mage willing to kill and charm for their own goals in called a Nphandus. If you want to make them really impactful make them something other then common human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 06-30-2018, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T15:34:39-07:00","id":1231462,"title":"","content":"A better, streamlined system like what Awakening inherited from Ascension, but done with Ascension's backstory in mind: these are people who somehow impose their will on reality, not exploit odd loopholes. Paradox needs to be better integrated, vulgar magick needs some good incentives to use it, and the system needs to get rid of 1's subtracting successes. Arete +Sphere would also probably help. And no more Avatar as the must-have Background to do anything consistently with magick. Maybe make the spheres cost less? Maybe reduce the number needed, if the game require so much interdependence with making magick? <br /> <br /> A more nuanced Technocracy-traditions battle, with both parties recognizing that they've been played for chumps by the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T15:36:31-07:00","id":1231463,"title":"","content":"Also, maybe not so much gratuitous shit as we saw in the early days of V5 would be nice. If we want it, we can add it. If we don't, then we don't need it taking up text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T22:09:26-07:00","id":1232050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1231309#post1231309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some backgrounds need to change.<br /> -Again on naphandi. right now every mage willing to kill and charm for their own goals in called a Nphandus. If you want to make them really impactful make them something other then common human.</div> </div> </div> </div>From which M:tA books did you get this incorrect idea ? As far as I know, only Mages who are part of the Nephandi faction are called Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T01:39:25-07:00","id":1232068,"title":"","content":"Yes. Technically, only Mages who went through the Cauls and got their Avatar inverted are Nephandi. Noone else.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are infernalists, psychopaths, murderers, psychological abusers, mind-controllers, con-artists..you name it, the Mage word probably has it, because they are human. But they are explicitely not Nephandi. And none of the Nephandic rules, Spheres etc. apply to them at all.<br /> Only those who went through the cauls are Nephandi. The rest are just bad people.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean, of course, that in-game both the Traditions and the Technocracy don't like to call Mages that they *really* want gone Nephandi, especially normal infernalists...but that is in-game propaganda. And that's perfectly fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-03-2018, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T06:47:29-07:00","id":1232105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232068#post1232068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Technically, only Mages who went through the Cauls and got their Avatar inverted are Nephandi. Noone else.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are infernalists, psychopaths, murderers, psychological abusers, mind-controllers, con-artists..you name it, the Mage word probably has it, because they are human. But they are explicitely not Nephandi. And none of the Nephandic rules, Spheres etc. apply to them at all.<br /> Only those who went through the cauls are Nephandi. The rest are just bad people.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean, of course, that in-game both the Traditions and the Technocracy don't like to call Mages that they *really* want gone Nephandi, especially normal infernalists...but that is in-game propaganda. And that's perfectly fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but M20 does point out that there are plenty of &quot;&quot;&quot;nephandi&quot;&quot;&quot; who aren't truly Nephandi. Mages and sorcerers who serve some Nephandus, or are being controlled by them, but don't quite fit the dictionary definition if you will. These are the Nephandi that most Mages will interact with and fight, if the real Nephandi are playing carefully and avoiding confrontation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T06:56:45-07:00","id":1232108,"title":"","content":"- Really carefully explained rules. Things should be clear for first time readers.<br /> <br /> - Time needs some new cool effect. Prime 5 lets you get rid of Paradox, which isn't an effect Prime needed to have. It's simply a magickal effect which writers justified as being part of Prime. Something similar for Time would be quite cool; hanging effects and conditional magick are examples, but the fact that Time shines well for Masters and Archmages (who have a bunch of sphere effects they can hang and set conditions for) but is relatively lackluster on its own is a problem. For all of Correspondence's synergy with the other Spheres, it still lets you teleport and conjure and perceive all around the world. Time, to me, feels like the Sphere that requires the most work and creativity to make it viable as an affinity sphere.<br /> <br /> - Make the Technocracy's punishments and activities more realistic. Nothing kills worker morale like people being blended up for dog food and replaced by a soulless clone which dies after 2 years. Traitors should be dealt with efficiently, not cruelly... assuming that the Technocracy isn't being controlled by the Nephandi. So essentially give a consistent vision of the &quot;kinder, gentler technocracy&quot;, one with great pensions and healthcare and opportunities for its employees, one where you can request memory censorship so you can retire with a glowing reference, one where there is a timetable for eradication of humanity's problems. Show a softer side to the Syndicate, one focused on the finances of charities and pensions and similar. Show an anti-corruption movement in the NWO which wants to reduce the emphasis on &quot;deep state&quot; and bring the Technocracy out of the shadows. Show a Technocracy where people can raise ideas without fear of being killed or punished, where dogma is less severe. And despite all of that, still remain critical of the Union's flaws, and all of the evil stuff it does even when it is at its best and most moral.<br /> <br /> For example, have really subtle and populist mind control being employed. Less Room 101 black site nonsense; you have enlightened science on your side, be subtle and charismatic! Carrot over stick. When betrayals and failures do occur, work with what you've got. A failure can be demoted, retrained, corrected with Mind, or their wages can be garnished to pay for semi-mandatory enhancements which will correct their failings. For example, a NWO agent who allows several reality deviants to escape them because of slow reflexes and poor fitness might be given minor enhancements and extensive conditioning/fitness training, with the relevant costs being deducted from their salary and the failure being placed in a file which is referenced when deciding on promotions and bonuses.<br /> <br /> Traitors might be executed, but this is less clandestine. Have new employees sign a contract stating that a Level X (or whatever) infraction of Union protocols, a malicious and deliberate betrayal of the Union, will lead to their apprehension and eventually to execution. But add some due process. Oversight from other Union employees, the chance to appeal unfair decisions, you get the idea. Make things a bit more transparent, with the necessary measures to keep sensitive intelligence under wraps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 07-03-2018, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T01:34:41-07:00","id":1232332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232050#post1232050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From which M:tA books did you get this incorrect idea ? As far as I know, only Mages who are part of the Nephandi faction are called Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically yes, however as I went through reading I didn't see any non-naphandy mages who would be &quot;infernalists, psychopaths, murderers, psychological abusers, mind-controllers, con-artists...&quot; and not have thrown in with the Terrible Forces of DOOM. Same with Demons and infernalists. What constitutes such formal 'evil' changes from culture to culture and through time. There should be some distinction for mages from the sleeper delusions.<br /> <br /> -As I like marauder presentation, one option I could come up with is to present naphandy in similar style. Only, instead of falling to general madness they fell into Quiet of nihilism and sociopathy, losing any capability for emphathy and affection, seeing whole creation as ugly affront. <br /> Service to outside powers is already represented by drawbacks like Fausitan Bargain that any mage can take and crimes (human sacrifice, etc.) should be handled on tradition-to-tradition and cultural bases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T06:36:26-07:00","id":1232359,"title":"","content":"It's true that non-Nephandi villans aren't so prevalent as one would think. Voormas it's the poster figure, but other than him...Well, we know they exist: There are whole factions depicted as &quot;evil by our standards&quot; out there, but few members of note. And it doesn't help that most of these factions are offensive stereotypes that one wouldn't want to touch with a ten foot pole, like the Aghori and Wu Keng<br /> <br /> It's also true that Nephandi could use a revision.<br /> <br /> I think that a paralel with Marauders it's a good idea: Rather than a cohesive faction with a very specific initiation ritual, Nephandi could trully be <i>fallen mages</i>. Usualy <i>to fall</i>, in a mystic sense, doesn't mean to join a nasty faction but rather to sucumb to risks or temptations inherent to being human while you're in the path of Ascencion. It's something that should be a risk regardless of your personal associations.<br /> <br /> Mages that face too much supernatural evil could end having a Marauder-like offering from their Avatars - one that wouldn't separate them from reality but rather adapt them to the evil of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:28:59-07:00","id":1232366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232359#post1232359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's true that non-Nephandi villans aren't so prevalent as one would think. Voormas it's the poster figure, but other than him...Well, we know they exist: There are whole factions depicted as &quot;evil by our standards&quot; out there, but few members of note. And it doesn't help that most of these factions are offensive stereotypes that one wouldn't want to touch with a ten foot pole, like the Aghori and Wu Keng<br /> <br /> It's also true that Nephandi could use a revision.<br /> <br /> I think that a paralel with Marauders it's a good idea: Rather than a cohesive faction with a very specific initiation ritual, Nephandi could trully be <i>fallen mages</i>. Usualy <i>to fall</i>, in a mystic sense, doesn't mean to join a nasty faction but rather to sucumb to risks or temptations inherent to being human while you're in the path of Ascencion. It's something that should be a risk regardless of your personal associations.<br /> <br /> Mages that face too much supernatural evil could end having a Marauder-like offering from their Avatars - one that wouldn't separate them from reality but rather adapt them to the evil of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>M5 could talk about organized Nephandi, the ones who collaborate to try and subvert sects and governments and try to cause mass descension, and the ones who operate alone or in small groups.<br /> <br /> Falling, going to the Cauls, should be demystified somewhat. You don't need an Evil Mentor to tell you to go to the Cauls, it's just something the Avatar tends to slip towards if you corrupt yourself enough. The idea would be that *any* Mage who behaves in a Nephandic manner can find the Cauls and choose to enter them, with their Avatar acting as a guide. It could even occur during a seeking or a quiet; if the Mage has become pessimistic about humanity and the state of the world, and has acted in a despicable and evil way, then it's possible a seeking or quiet might end up bringing them to the Cauls and giving them the opportunity to invert their Avatar.<br /> <br /> This is a almost a moot point since Nephandi are meant to be NPCs, but falling could grant a &quot;&quot;&quot;free&quot;&quot;&quot; dot of Arete, Entropy or Spirit, or even all three. Actual tangible power should come from falling, to underline a key tragedy of Mage (power being a complete red herring when it comes to Ascension, and Archmages being people who have lost their way and become too obsessed with power over enlightenment).<br /> <br /> It could add in a bit about Fallen mages tending to recognize eachother (a unique Perception + Awareness roll might be a good trait to represent this advantage) to explain how Nephandi organize and form societies in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 07-04-2018, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T09:50:08-07:00","id":1232413,"title":"","content":"Book of Secrets mentions a new kind of Marauder that's based on Denial rather than Madness (the Negation Men). I wouldn't mind seeing the Nephandi redefined in terms of Morbidity in a somewhat similar manner, and saying that the business about going to the Cauls is just a means of forcing someone into a state of permanent Morbidity. So going to the Cauls still makes you a Nephandus, but it's no longer the only way to become one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:40:01-07:00","id":1232435,"title":"","content":"Indeed, albeit the Negation Men themselves could use a little more development, I would like the Static mages to be, if not as diverse, at least as developed as their Dynamic counterparts. Right now they're kinda boring<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232366#post1232366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M5 could talk about organized Nephandi, the ones who collaborate to try and subvert sects and governments and try to cause mass descension, and the ones who operate alone or in small groups.<br /> <br /> Falling, going to the Cauls, should be demystified somewhat. You don't need an Evil Mentor to tell you to go to the Cauls, it's just something the Avatar tends to slip towards if you corrupt yourself enough. The idea would be that *any* Mage who behaves in a Nephandic manner can find the Cauls and choose to enter them, with their Avatar acting as a guide. It could even occur during a seeking or a quiet; if the Mage has become pessimistic about humanity and the state of the world, and has acted in a despicable and evil way, then it's possible a seeking or quiet might end up bringing them to the Cauls and giving them the opportunity to invert their Avatar.<br /> <br /> This is a almost a moot point since Nephandi are meant to be NPCs, but falling could grant a &quot;&quot;&quot;free&quot;&quot;&quot; dot of Arete, Entropy or Spirit, or even all three. Actual tangible power should come from falling, to underline a key tragedy of Mage (power being a complete red herring when it comes to Ascension, and Archmages being people who have lost their way and become too obsessed with power over enlightenment).<br /> <br /> It could add in a bit about Fallen mages tending to recognize eachother (a unique Perception + Awareness roll might be a good trait to represent this advantage) to explain how Nephandi organize and form societies in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> Inverted Avatars may also have a special affinity for evil spirits and spooks, allowing to recognize them and their urges with the same Awareness roll. Perhaps demons and specters could treat them as &quot;kindred spirits&quot; / &quot;one of us&quot;.<br /> That way the fallen mages would have an easier time seeking knowledge and power on dark places (and surviving to tell the tale). This would explain why Nephandi always seem to be related to demons and other spooks when they aren't more prone to make pacts than any other mage (actually, they're less inclined to do so - but then, having insight on demonic agendas may also help at avoiding unwanted bonds)<br /> <br /> Fallen &quot;Traditions&quot;, like the adorers of the Wyrm or Cthulhu cultists, could be merely factions that favor falling. Perhaps even worshiping the Fallen among their members. They would make a point in indulging in every nasty practice <i>rumored </i>to get you there, but most of their members would be normal non-Nephandi dark/bad mages (much like most of the Sabbat follows Humanity).<br /> This would preserve the idea of &quot;fake Nephandi wanabe&quot; and also the idea that old and potent Nephandi Cthulhu cults do, indeed, exist (even if they sometimes embarrass the Aswadim).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T11:35:51-07:00","id":1232456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232413#post1232413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of Secrets mentions a new kind of Marauder that's based on Denial rather than Madness (the Negation Men). I wouldn't mind seeing the Nephandi redefined in terms of Morbidity in a somewhat similar manner, and saying that the business about going to the Cauls is just a means of forcing someone into a state of permanent Morbidity. So going to the Cauls still makes you a Nephandus, but it's no longer the only way to become one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I adore the Negation Men. I really want to have a plot about a powerful Mage manipulating and creating Negation men using extensive and subtle psychic conditioning, as a weapon against the Technocracy and the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T11:39:55-07:00","id":1232457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232435#post1232435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed.<br /> <br /> Inverted Avatars may also have a special affinity for evil spirits and spooks, allowing to recognize them and their urges with the same Awareness roll. Perhaps demons and specters could treat them as &quot;kindred spirits&quot; / &quot;one of us&quot;.<br /> That way the fallen mages would have an easier time seeking knowledge and power on dark places (and surviving to tell the tale). This would explain why Nephandi always seem to be related to demons and other spooks when they aren't more prone to make pacts than any other mage (actually, they're less inclined to do so - but then, having insight on demonic agendas may also help at avoiding unwanted bonds)<br /> <br /> Fallen &quot;Traditions&quot;, like the adorers of the Wyrm or Cthulhu cultists, could be merely factions that favor falling. Perhaps even worshiping the Fallen among their members. They would make a point in indulging in every nasty practice <i>rumored </i>to get you there, but most of their members would be normal non-Nephandi dark/bad mages (much like most of the Sabbat follows Humanity).<br /> This would preserve the idea of &quot;fake Nephandi wanabe&quot; and also the idea that old and potent Nephandi Cthulhu cults do, indeed, exist (even if they sometimes embarrass the Aswadim).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, imagine if you introduced the idea from a Hermetic perspective, someone with a big focus on Angels vs. Fallen Angels.<br /> <br /> &quot;Mages have a shard of the divine in them. A little bit of The One. An angel, or something like that. That's the Avatar, our magickal core, the spiritual force that allows us to change reality. And we all know that angels have fallen before. Spirits can become corrupted and broken. The Nephandi are Mages whose wickedness and selfishness has caused their own inner angel to fall, along with those unfortunate enough to inherit such broken Avatars. They become inverted, seeking Descension rather than Ascension, and they form some of the most formidable and terrible foes a Magus can face.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then introduce mechanics for Nephandi recognising Demons (fallen angels), other Nephandi (those with inverted Avatars), Banes and similar (dark spirits which they have an affinity for), and mechanics for them bonding more easily socially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T00:14:45-07:00","id":1232570,"title":"","content":"Now, these are some great ideas, take all the 'likes' XD<br /> Although, I propose making Caul a specific type of Mystery Play that mage undergoes rather then an actual place. A true damnation is always within you after all. <br /> <br /> on the other hand, this way it gives a better foundation for naphandi infiltration of the Technocracy. Science after all doesn't really give the moral bedrock necessary to resist the fall that comes from within the mage himself, rather then objective outside sources.<br /> As Traditions often suffer from not being practical enough, so must the technocracy for having no spirituality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 07-05-2018, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T03:15:30-07:00","id":1232580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232105#post1232105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, but M20 does point out that there are plenty of &quot;&quot;&quot;nephandi&quot;&quot;&quot; who aren't truly Nephandi. Mages and sorcerers who serve some Nephandus, or are being controlled by them, but don't quite fit the dictionary definition if you will. These are the Nephandi that most Mages will interact with and fight, if the real Nephandi are playing carefully and avoiding confrontation.</div> </div> </div> </div>( Sorcerers can't be Nephandi. A person needs to be a Mage to be a Nephandus. ) If a Nephandus or a group of Nephandi manipulate or deal with some persons to the point of having them as ( for example ) retainers, this does not make those persons Nephandi in any sense ; such retainers aren't part of the Nephandi at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232366#post1232366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Falling, going to the Cauls, should be demystified somewhat. You don't need an Evil Mentor to tell you to go to the Cauls (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>According to what is written in the Book of Madness 2nd edition, only Nephandi can initiate others into the Nephandi - only they have the means to do so.<br /> Also, there are various ways of being initiated into the Nephandi - those that choose to be part of the Malfean Nephandi walk ( or dance ) the Black Spiral ; while potential Infernal Nephandi make infernal pacts and/or deals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-05-2018, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T07:01:25-07:00","id":1232613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232570#post1232570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, I propose making Caul a specific type of Mystery Play that mage undergoes rather then an actual place. A true damnation is always within you after all.<br /> <br /> on the other hand, this way it gives a better foundation for naphandi infiltration of the Technocracy. Science after all doesn't really give the moral bedrock necessary to resist the fall that comes from within the mage himself, rather then objective outside sources.<br /> As Traditions often suffer from not being practical enough, so must the technocracy for having no spirituality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...that would be good.<br /> <br /> Albeit I would still keep places that are sacred for the anti-initiation - so to speak. Like the Black Spiral. They would be rare and dangeous places where the chances of falling (or dying while resisting the fall) become almost certain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Did</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to what is written in the Book of Madness 2nd edition, only Nephandi can initiate others into the Nephandi - only they have the means to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the idea would be to change that in order to make Damnation more personal and the Fall something that can happen to anyone regardless of personal relationships with evil mages of evil.<br /> <br /> Of course, Nephandi would still work to utterly corrupt mages, and corrupt mages would have a tendency to fall. Even if they don't, they would still be eroding the foundations of their own factions with their corruption, which also helps Nephandi.<br /> <br /> The way Cauls are right now, they work as a &quot;Nephandic room 101&quot;. They're a standard item included in every Labyrinth worth it's salt That way they become just another iteration of: &quot;mage has been sequestered - let's rescue him before the enemy converts them&quot;. To make descent a &quot;room 101 situation, just worse 'cause this it's forever&quot; impedes to trully play with all the dark concepts of a damnation story:<br /> If you got pushed, then all there's to your falling it's that someone pushed you and you weren't able to avoid it. If you fall by your own merit there's a lot of things that could have influenced the fall, lots of potential motives for your ultimate choice, and a lot of influences that could have saved your soul but didn't. I feel stories about damnation/salvation get cheapened if they are literal rescue missions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-05-2018, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T08:58:28-07:00","id":1232633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232580#post1232580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">( Sorcerers can't be Nephandi. A person needs to be a Mage to be a Nephandus. ) If a Nephandus or a group of Nephandi manipulate or deal with some persons to the point of having them as ( for example ) retainers, this does not make those persons Nephandi in any sense ; such retainers aren't part of the Nephandi at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> According to what is written in the Book of Madness 2nd edition, only Nephandi can initiate others into the Nephandi - only they have the means to do so.<br /> Also, there are various ways of being initiated into the Nephandi - those that choose to be part of the Malfean Nephandi walk ( or dance ) the Black Spiral ; while potential Infernal Nephandi make infernal pacts and/or deals.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20, when talking about the Nephandi, makes it clear that many so-called Nephandi aren't truly Nephandi; the pawns of Nephandi are often misinterpreted as those who are pulling the strings. These puppets include infernalists of all stripes.<br /> <br /> That's true; this thread is about potential changes being made in M5 which would improve the system. Personally I think that Falling should always be a risk, and that any Mage should have the potential to enter the Cauls. This shouldn't require a Sith Lord tempting you to go skinny dipping in an anti-reality jacuzzi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T11:02:45-07:00","id":1234049,"title":"","content":"I also think that Foci, Blatancy and use of Mythic Threads should be united in one coherent system. <br /> <br /> It is quite logical. If you learn some subject you also know what constitutes popular perception of it and with some quick think (Wits + Ability roll?) could mask magic under it. <br /> <br /> So you, a hermetic, have Art: Painting as foci, 3 Mind and want to make a picture that entrances the audience.<br /> <br /> Roll 1: Intelligence + Occult for proper mystic designs<br /> Roll 2: Wits + Art for hiding occult features under appropriate painting features<br /> Roll 3: Dexterity + Art for Actually painting it. <br /> <br /> Result: an entrancing picture that may make you look at it for hours lost in thought. Need to overcome second roll successes to determine it's supernatural without magical senses. <br /> <br /> This is just an approximate proposition. I just think these features should be integrated in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T23:04:47-07:00","id":1235190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1234049#post1234049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that Foci, Blatancy and use of Mythic Threads should be united in one coherent system.<br /> <br /> It is quite logical. If you learn some subject you also know what constitutes popular perception of it and with some quick think (Wits + Ability roll?) could mask magic under it.<br /> <br /> So you, a hermetic, have Art: Painting as foci, 3 Mind and want to make a picture that entrances the audience.<br /> <br /> Roll 1: Intelligence + Occult for proper mystic designs<br /> Roll 2: Wits + Art for hiding occult features under appropriate painting features<br /> Roll 3: Dexterity + Art for Actually painting it.<br /> <br /> Result: an entrancing picture that may make you look at it for hours lost in thought. Need to overcome second roll successes to determine it's supernatural without magical senses.<br /> <br /> This is just an approximate proposition. I just think these features should be integrated in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't Roll 1 be somehow made together with rolling the casting Mage's Arete ? I think that it is inseparateable for at the very least most Mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1232613#post1232613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the idea would be to change that in order to make Damnation more personal and the Fall something that can happen to anyone regardless of personal relationships with evil mages of evil.<br /> <br /> Of course, Nephandi would still work to utterly corrupt mages, and corrupt mages would have a tendency to fall. Even if they don't, they would still be eroding the foundations of their own factions with their corruption, which also helps Nephandi.<br /> <br /> The way Cauls are right now, they work as a &quot;Nephandic room 101&quot;. They're a standard item included in every Labyrinth worth it's salt That way they become just another iteration of: &quot;mage has been sequestered - let's rescue him before the enemy converts them&quot;. To make descent a &quot;room 101 situation, just worse 'cause this it's forever&quot; impedes to trully play with all the dark concepts of a damnation story:<br /> If you got pushed, then all there's to your falling it's that someone pushed you and you weren't able to avoid it. If you fall by your own merit there's a lot of things that could have influenced the fall, lots of potential motives for your ultimate choice, and a lot of influences that could have saved your soul but didn't. I feel stories about damnation/salvation get cheapened if they are literal rescue missions...</div> </div> </div> </div>Within this idea that you have, would becoming a Nephandi Mage be a decision that can't be turned back, as it is suggested in some parts of what is currently written about the Nephandi in M:tA books ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T00:37:39-07:00","id":1235210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1235190#post1235190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Roll 1 be somehow made together with rolling the casting Mage's Arete ? I think that it is inseparateable for at the very least most Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>you are right. I think it should be on roll 3 though. because it's then when you actually create the effect. so it would be <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dexterity + Art </span></span></span></div>+ Arete?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T00:43:04-07:00","id":1235211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Within this idea that you have, would becoming a Nephandi Mage be a decision that can't be turned back, as it is suggested in some parts of what is currently written about the Nephandi in M:tA books ? </div> </div> </div>Probably. This alternate view of Nephandi is similar to the Marauders; and once you\u2019ve gone Marauder, there\u2019s no going back. Likewise, once a mage takes that crucial step into Nephandi-hood, the equivalent of picking up your first point of perma-Madness, that\u2019s it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T01:51:00-07:00","id":1235217,"title":"","content":"I'd like Ascension to move away from presenting the Technocracy as obviously wrong and evil. The whole setting of the Ascension War is based on the premise that reality is a clash of differing ideas. Presenting one of the main parties as &quot;bad&quot; invalidates the entire premise for me. Focus less on TU atrocities (though they should still be there) and highlight all the good they are doing some more. At the same time devote some word count to why the Traditions are in their way horrible people sometimes aswell. The base assumption of MtA should not be &quot;here are the traditions, those are the good guys&quot; it should be &quot;many mages strive to make the world better but no two of them can agree how to do it. Where do you stand?&quot;. Crafts, Traditions, Orphans and Technocrats should be designed as equally player appealing options, their organizations all having good and bad aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T03:02:26-07:00","id":1235224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1235217#post1235217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole setting of the Ascension War is based on the premise that reality is a clash of differing ideas. Presenting one of the main parties as &quot;bad&quot; invalidates the entire premise for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the premise. The Ascension War is deliberately cast as a pointless war that distracts mages from doing anything useful.<br /> <br /> Equalising the Technocracy with the others would totally hollow them out as an idea. The point is that they're a systemic power structure in the way the other factions aren't, it's a contrasting style of game. Also, the Traditions explicitly aren't the good guys, (I mean, the mass murder of their leadership is presented as largely a good thing) they're simply not as morally compromised as the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T04:53:26-07:00","id":1235244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1235224#post1235224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the premise. The Ascension War is deliberately cast as a pointless war that distracts mages from doing anything useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do not argue that cooperation would lead to a more successful implementation of one particular paradigm than the clash of visions the Ascension War is... what useful things would they do weren't they so distracted? The Ascension War is pretty much it if you look at the grand scheme of things, the alternative would be aforementioned implementation of a unified paradigm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T07:16:04-07:00","id":1235263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1235244#post1235244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do not argue that cooperation would lead to a more successful implementation of one particular paradigm than the clash of visions the Ascension War is... what useful things would they do weren't they so distracted? The Ascension War is pretty much it if you look at the grand scheme of things, the alternative would be aforementioned implementation of a unified paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>End world hunger? Heal people? Teach people useful technology? Pretty much what the Technocracy has done. Like, the Technocracy have got more or less the right aim, it's that their implementation is counterproductive. They don't actually need a unified paradigm, they just think they do.<br /> <br /> You've also missed the option that the Traditions propose, let paradigms co-exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T13:03:44-07:00","id":1235315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1235263#post1235263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't actually need a unified paradigm, they just think they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to Paradox they sort of do, as the Sleepers have to accept their methods of doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You've also missed the option that the Traditions propose, let paradigms co-exist. </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think that's really a realistic option. You can make the &quot;purple paradigm&quot; king, but that is in itself a specific paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T21:04:41-07:00","id":1235414,"title":"","content":"Yes; but its defining feature is that it meshes well with a diverse selection of other paradigms that otherwise wouldn't be able to coexist, and provides an interface between them that lets them work together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T06:55:10-07:00","id":1235534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within this idea that you have, would becoming a Nephandi Mage be a decision that can't be turned back, as it is suggested in some parts of what is currently written about the Nephandi in M:tA books ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Dataweaver said, establishing a parallelism with Marauderdom makes it permanent.<br /> <br /> However, if I were to write a whole book about them, I would like to play with the idea of redemption. Redemption stories it's a genre that's very much in-paradigm for many Traditions. It shoulnd't be easy though. <i>Damnation </i>it's too strong of a word for something that can be turned back just 'cause you want:<br /> <br /> *Perhaps there's a middle ground between being a normal mage and becoming a Nephandi - a moment where the Caul becomes possible but the mage hasn't fallen yet, and this moments could seed redemption stories (and if the players botch or don't care the character falls and can't be turned back)<br /> *If vampires have legendas about curing The Curse of Caine, there could be similar legends for curing Nephandi - but this would require the Nephandi to be willing to change. Something supposed to be impossible. Perhaps, like Marauders, Nephandi have levels of madness and thus their evil can be ameliorated - perhaps to the point of feeling a little remorse in the lowest level. But it shouldn't be easy. Not any easier than curing Marauders anyway.<br /> *Perhaps the mage who <i>chose </i>to fall can't be redeemed but the inheritors of their inverted avatars can, if approached soon enough. Having a twisted avatar could be a Flaw that damns your mage to the Fall unless you can attain this legendary cure first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-16-2018, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T13:45:36-07:00","id":1236883,"title":"","content":"Get rid of the Disparate Alliance.<br /> <br /> Keep the individual Crafts, but the Disparate Alliance was one of the reasons why I did not like M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T21:47:22-07:00","id":1239196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1228392#post1228392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I let it buff things that require perfect timing, dancing, music.. shooting people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is very useful for a wide range of Abilities and situations. Two other effects that I haven't seen talked about but seem reasonable for Time 1: remembering anything you've experienced directly; and knowing how old a currently existing (and within sensory range) object, creature, or process is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T02:39:00-07:00","id":1249086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1235217#post1235217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like Ascension to move away from presenting the Technocracy as obviously wrong and evil. The whole setting of the Ascension War is based on the premise that reality is a clash of differing ideas. Presenting one of the main parties as &quot;bad&quot; invalidates the entire premise for me. Focus less on TU atrocities (though they should still be there) and highlight all the good they are doing some more. At the same time devote some word count to why the Traditions are in their way horrible people sometimes aswell. The base assumption of MtA should not be &quot;here are the traditions, those are the good guys&quot; it should be &quot;many mages strive to make the world better but no two of them can agree how to do it. Where do you stand?&quot;. Crafts, Traditions, Orphans and Technocrats should be designed as equally player appealing options, their organizations all having good and bad aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they've been doing that for about the last 20 years in one way or another. <br /> <br /> The problem I see, for any prospective 5th Edition Mage if they base it on the design features of Vampire 5th, is that they will need to tailor it back a little. This means, for me, only having the Nine Traditions plus maybe Orphans (or Hollow Ones?) in the core book. A lot of players seem to be enampred for playing Technocracy agents. Mage Revised (3rd Edition) tried to tailor it back in such a way, although it had criticism, while also trying to integrate some of the Crafts as factions in the Traditions. There is some virtue in this approach, but ultimately, I think the game will need to be more focussed than the 20th Anniversary (or 4th Edition). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T06:11:32-07:00","id":1249104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1249086#post1249086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I see, for any prospective 5th Edition Mage if they base it on the design features of Vampire 5th, is that they will need to tailor it back a little. This means, for me, only having the Nine Traditions plus maybe Orphans (or Hollow Ones?) in the core book. A lot of players seem to be enampred for playing Technocracy agents. Mage Revised (3rd Edition) tried to tailor it back in such a way, although it had criticism, while also trying to integrate some of the Crafts as factions in the Traditions. There is some virtue in this approach, but ultimately, I think the game will need to be more focussed than the 20th Anniversary (or 4th Edition).</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, if you have rules to play Orphans and the Focus rules/fluff of M20 you can remake every Tradition and Convention with just a little more fluff. No need to port special Disciplines and weaknesses for each one of them, nor to go into detail in the Basic. The exeption would be the alternate spheres of the Technocracy, but they can be covered in the writeup of the 9 Spheres (they mostly represent minor mechanical changes, except PU which introduces a new Quintessence source)<br /> <br /> I think that the modifications of the magick system are what will make or break M5. It was what made Mage popular in the first place, after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T13:06:27-07:00","id":1249199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1249104#post1249104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, if you have rules to play Orphans and the Focus rules/fluff of M20 you can remake every Tradition and Convention with just a little more fluff. No need to port special Disciplines and weaknesses for each one of them, nor to go into detail in the Basic. The exeption would be the alternate spheres of the Technocracy, but they can be covered in the writeup of the 9 Spheres (they mostly represent minor mechanical changes, except PU which introduces a new Quintessence source)<br /> <br /> I think that the modifications of the magick system are what will make or break M5. It was what made Mage popular in the first place, after all</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they would need to rewrite Forces a little, as it's poorly defined currently (talking about Greek Elements, rather than the interactions between matter which it should be about). I also hope they will re-think the Order of Hermes supposed association with Forces as it has never really fit with their actual paradigm and Tradition. You are right though, in terms of designing characters, you just need to establish the choice of nine Spheres in different combinations and have a series of readiliy available Paradigms. If we follow the model of V5, then instead of Predator types, you could have a list of Paradigms to choose from (based on the ones given in M20). An Orphan could, essentially represent any Craft after this point. <br /> <br /> I honestly think that the Technocracy would have to have their own book. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T15:04:52-07:00","id":1249219,"title":"","content":"<i>p a r a d o x<br /> <br /> d i c e</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T15:07:59-07:00","id":1249223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1249219#post1249219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>p a r a d o x<br /> <br /> d i c e</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, as much as I dislike V5 (I enjoy the ideas but dislike the application immensely), I think M5 could be a great addition, if only for ideas to peruse.<br /> <br /> For example, if in M5 there were some neat benefit to Time 1 which doesn't exist in M20 then it would be nice to bring it over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T06:54:17-07:00","id":1249377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1249223#post1249223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, as much as I dislike V5 (I enjoy the ideas but dislike the application immensely), I think M5 could be a great addition, if only for ideas to peruse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, then let's hope we won't dislike the application immensely this time :P<br /> <br /> I want to see what will they come up to. Dynamic Magick was quite a novel concept when Mage was first launched but time has pass and lots of systems like that have been developed. I'm sure there's a lot of mechanics that can be improved. Time 1 it's but a small example: <i>real </i>Rote rules, more reliable rules regarding necessary successes (can it be that in the future we will be able to answer accurately when someone asks how hard its to do something in this game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), Paradox dice (they were always dice, but not this way). Paradigms as some sort of &quot;predator types&quot; sounds pretty neat too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:01:47-07:00","id":1249383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1249377#post1249377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, then let's hope we won't dislike the application immensely this time :P<br /> <br /> I want to see what will they come up to. Dynamic Magick was quite a novel concept when Mage was first launched but time has pass and lots of systems like that have been developed. I'm sure there's a lot of mechanics that can be improved. Time 1 it's but a small example: <i>real </i>Rote rules, more reliable rules regarding necessary successes (can it be that in the future we will be able to answer accurately when someone asks how hard its to do something in this game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), Paradox dice (they were always dice, but not this way). Paradigms as some sort of &quot;predator types&quot; sounds pretty neat too</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Paradox Dice which are added to certain Arete rolls would feel quite appropriate. So if you have a Paradox of 10 hanging over you, you might feel like you shouldn't risk using any more magick, in case that finally sets off your Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T01:45:27-07:00","id":1249644,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Paradox Dice, but it would have to take some work to ensure that any changes were properly integrated into the Mage gameplay. We don't want a setting being shoe-horned into an existing type of system - we want a system to emulate the concepts of the setting. Then again, I do sometimes feel that the Quintessence/Paradox wheel that is currently used is a bit vague, so a more concrete set of rules that make Paradox effects more dramatic and imaginative would be great. <br /> <br /> With regards to the Spheres, I feel they could definitily be reworked in some cases, even changed. However, my personal drive would be to accentuate the freeform nature rather than stipulate more rules and definition. It was this that ultimately made me feel that Mage: The Awakening was too rule heavy in its magic. I'd actually try to encourage players to move away from Rote casting, towards a more broad application of Spheres and then make the various effects more intuitive to remember in a game concept (less rule book referencing). This may be tricky of course!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T03:31:15-07:00","id":1249659,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Paradox Dice as well. Though with what I have in mind, they'd not replace paradox points. They handle backlashes.<br /> <br /> A way I can see it working, off the top of my head, is:<br /> <br /> * Paradox accumulation (1 for vulgar without witnesses, more for botches, etc.) works as usual M20 rules.<br /> * After(!) every time you perform a Vulgar magic roll (or botch on coincidental), one of the Arete die gets replaced by a Paradox die for further vulgar(!) rolls. This accumulates.<br /> * On a '0' on a paradox die, you get a backlash, and the paradox dice get replaced with normal dice again.<br /> <br /> That way you can have streaks of using vulgar magic without any backlash happening - but paradox accumulates - or you can have a series of quick discharges with low paradox amounts. Up to Lady Luck.<br /> Either way, after a backlash the next arete roll won't have any paradox dice. It's up to the mage to risk gaining some again while they possibly have a pile of paradox left.<br /> <br /> As an optional system, it also takes the 'responsibility' of deciding on a blacklash or no-backlash away from the ST. Food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T07:18:53-07:00","id":1249695,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> I like your idea.<br /> <br /> To elaborate on that:<br /> <br /> Botching on a Coincidental effect could provide a dice too. That way casting only Coincident stuff isn't entirely safe<br /> <br /> Instead of rolling yet more Paradox dice to determine the severity of the Backlash, the result of the dice could indicate the seriousness and amount of Paradox dots used to determine the backlash. Like one 0, lvl 1-5 Backlash, two 0 lvl 1-10 Backlash and so on - this it's too lenient because 0s are rare unless you have a ton of dice, but I think it could work arround these lines. <br /> <br /> There could be some way to avoid that result. For instance, expend a point of Willpower to reroll one or more Paradox Dice, to have a chance to stop or mitigate the backlash (but if it's stoped then you don't loose your dice nor your dots). That way doing magick to cleanse your dice it's less risky and more dependant of player's input. <hr /><br /> However I think the dice are going to seek to replace the dots because they're following V5 game design - to avoid &quot;gas tanks&quot;...I'm not agaist the idea, but I have yet to think on a way to trully replace the dots.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you could sum the result of the Paradox dice to determine the severity in a table (with &quot;nothing happens&quot; for results from 1-5)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-29-2018, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T07:28:10-07:00","id":1249696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1249644#post1249644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Paradox Dice, but it would have to take some work to ensure that any changes were properly integrated into the Mage gameplay. We don't want a setting being shoe-horned into an existing type of system - we want a system to emulate the concepts of the setting. Then again, I do sometimes feel that the Quintessence/Paradox wheel that is currently used is a bit vague, so a more concrete set of rules that make Paradox effects more dramatic and imaginative would be great. <br /> <br /> With regards to the Spheres, I feel they could definitily be reworked in some cases, even changed. However, my personal drive would be to accentuate the freeform nature rather than stipulate more rules and definition. It was this that ultimately made me feel that Mage: The Awakening was too rule heavy in its magic. I'd actually try to encourage players to move away from Rote casting, towards a more broad application of Spheres and then make the various effects more intuitive to remember in a game concept (less rule book referencing). This may be tricky of course!<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. The free form of magic is what makes Mage different. No spell lists or anything like that. We dont use rotes and never have. When we first started playing Mage I had made 2 rotes for each player and their immediate response was that the whole appeal of Mage was no spell lists so why did they need rotes. That was the end of that and we've never felt that we were missing a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T07:40:48-07:00","id":1249698,"title":"","content":"Arete probably needs changing to implement a Paradox Dice system. I'm not <i>entirely </i>OK, conceptually, with having more chances to Backlash the bigger it's your Arete pool.<br /> <br /> Surely it can be justified but the old system never intended your chances of getting Paradox to be directly proportional to your Enligthenment (that having a higher dicepool increased the chances of Botching was solved in Revised - no need to bring that back.)<br /> <br /> There could be some way to balance this:<br /> <br /> Perhaps dusting the old rule that allowed you to roll less dice than you need to cast an effect: Say, if you have Arete 6 and 4 Paradox Dice, you can choose to forfeit 4 dice to null your Backlash chances (until you get more 'dox dice) - of course, then you're casting with a meager Arete 2.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps something nasty happens when your 'dox dice fill your entire Arete poll - and thus having a bigger pool (with a bigger chance to Backlash) has it's advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T10:03:37-07:00","id":1249721,"title":"","content":"What's this \u201cparadigms as predator types\u201d thing?<br /> <br /> Another possibility for Paradox Dice might be to let the mage voluntarily add some to a Vulgar casting pool, on top of the dice he'd normally get. Similar to Awakening 2e's concept of Paradox bring the result of overextending yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T12:59:21-07:00","id":1249758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1249659#post1249659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Paradox Dice as well. Though with what I have in mind, they'd not replace paradox points. They handle backlashes.<br /> <br /> A way I can see it working, off the top of my head, is:<br /> <br /> * Paradox accumulation (1 for vulgar without witnesses, more for botches, etc.) works as usual M20 rules.<br /> * After(!) every time you perform a Vulgar magic roll (or botch on coincidental), one of the Arete die gets replaced by a Paradox die for further vulgar(!) rolls. This accumulates.<br /> * On a '0' on a paradox die, you get a backlash, and the paradox dice get replaced with normal dice again.<br /> <br /> That way you can have streaks of using vulgar magic without any backlash happening - but paradox accumulates - or you can have a series of quick discharges with low paradox amounts. Up to Lady Luck.<br /> Either way, after a backlash the next arete roll won't have any paradox dice. It's up to the mage to risk gaining some again while they possibly have a pile of paradox left.<br /> <br /> As an optional system, it also takes the 'responsibility' of deciding on a blacklash or no-backlash away from the ST. Food for thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd definitely be glad to have a system like this. Right now whether you backlash feels somewhat arbitrary.<br /> <br /> An alteration though; perhaps when you backlash, you only remove the paradox dice which fell on 1s; the other remain.<br /> <br /> So for example, Sarah is running with 10 points of Paradox, and has 3 paradox dice and 5 arete. When she tries to turn a person who is attacking her into autumn leaves so they can blow away in the wind, with a simple look and the word &quot;die&quot;, she rolls her 5 dice. 2 normal dice and 3 paradox dice.<br /> <br /> She succeeds, getting 4 successes (Willpower + 4 successes and a botch die). The botch die is a paradox die, so she then suffers a backlash. From here it's the same as M20.<br /> <br /> But next vulgar roll she does in this scene, she still has 3 paradox dice. This is because only one was removed by her backlash, and one was added for performing a vulgar roll.<br /> <br /> If two of her paradox dice had come up as 1s, then she would have rolled for backlash in a way which is somehow worse; perhaps discharging more at once on top of the result of the normal roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T18:05:18-07:00","id":1249850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1249721#post1249721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's this \u201cparadigms as predator types\u201d thing?<br /> <br /> Another possibility for Paradox Dice might be to let the mage voluntarily add some to a Vulgar casting pool, on top of the dice he'd normally get. Similar to Awakening 2e's concept of Paradox bring the result of overextending yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just a speculative idea at the moment of course, but in M20 there are a a number of common paradigms of magic listed - &quot;A Mechanical Universe&quot; or &quot;Everything is data&quot; or &quot;Everything is an Illusion&quot; and so on. I think we could use these as a core aspect on the character sheet, in the same way a vampire lists &quot;Predator&quot; type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 08-29-2018, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T07:55:54-07:00","id":1257365,"title":"","content":"I would like to see something like this brought into M5.<br /> <br /> Paradox could be rated 1-5 like hunger and a thing that would give you paradox could be a paradox check to see if the universe took notice. If you fail you gain a level of paradox if you succeed you don't. Paradox can bleed out at any time not just on magic rolls. You try to contain it for as long as you can so you can bleed it normally but sometimes it doesn't work out that way. Every time you roll you add paradox dice and on a paradox failure your pattern takes damage but you continue to hold it in. The amount of superficial damage is equal to your paradox level. If you roll a critical win and one of the 10's is on your paradox dice you suffer a backlash with a severity equal to your paradox level. The only way to remove paradox is with an action of some sort, each tradition has a way that they fool reality into accepting them and this is known as paradigm. Paradigm is used to lower your paradox level. All mages know that everything is possible and that any mage can use their spheres to the full extent but when you channel your magic through paradigm you lesson realities chance at catching you (vulgar/coincidental) or take realities scrutiny off of you (remove paradox levels).<br /> <br /> Basically I would like to either have a better understanding of paradigm or to have it work more cohesively when it comes to mechanics and fluff. I would also love paradox dice that make paradox something that is more punishing to a mage. Mages can control the universe and I think that without paradigm and paradox they should have just dominated the WoD long ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T09:00:52-07:00","id":1257378,"title":"","content":"While I agree with the general idea, 5 levels and a fast progression could be a little too tight to compress all the punishment that Paradox represents.<br /> <br /> Vampires can survive a Frenzy and keep playing, Mages sent to a Paradox Realm are, at the very least, out of the story for good. It's all nice and good to say that Paradox should be punishing, but making it's upper echelons as frequent or nearly so as Vampire frenzy it's overkill<br /> <br /> Perhaps you could multiply your level by the amount of critical successes/botches and then compare with a table. Like: 5 crits with 5 'dox dice and you're sent to a Realm (well, that's going to the other end of the spectrum - making such outcome too unlikely - but the general idea it's to have a wider margin).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-26-2018, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T10:58:32-07:00","id":1257401,"title":"","content":"Yes my desires for the system also included a way for the PCs to mitigate or remove paradox by doing an action related to the characters paradigm. What that action or actions are would be up for discussion but it is similar to feeding for vampires they can reduce their hunger by feeding. A universal action could be to bleed the paradox off causing aggravated damage to yourself on a one for one bases. This means that the PCs are slightly in control of wether or not they go to a realm.<br /> <br /> Paradox also only rises half the time since it is a paradox check so this is effective of a 10 dot paradox system but statistical runs can happen for or against the character. This is the fickle nature of the universe but if you see that you are on a run of gaining paradox you should know that the universe is watching you closely and adjust your actions accordingly. One way you can do this is by using magic in a more coincidental manor which is another aspect of your paradigm. Each tradition could have several paradigms to choose form that represent factions within the tradition.<br /> <br /> To go to a realm a character would have to make the decision to allow their paradox to grow out of control, not take an action to reduce it or take action to mitigate its growth, not spend will to help contain it through re-rolls and the like, allow it to grow further and take a chance that they will not messy cirt at some point. They are literally tempting fate and that is OK with me if they fail at that point since they made the choices that led them to the realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T15:14:55-07:00","id":1257455,"title":"","content":"I just hope that you don\u00b4t get a paradox check becuase you don\u00b4t need it at all.You are already rolling to see if the spell works or not.<br /> <br /> Just give the character paradox points equal to the level of the sphere involved when he fails a roll wich will become more posible if you are going against the consensus ,you roll your paradox as a dicepool to get the result when you reach 5 or better 10 becuase paradox is a bigger penalty than hunger and becuase active spells (Each one gives you one permanent paradox , the number of active spells is limited by your arete/gnosis).The next is an example of how the result of the roll may be interpretated<br /> <br /> 0 Absolved The Universe may love you becuase paradox has left you untouched.<br /> 1-2 Caught The Universe has seen you mess with the natural order , you fool , one of yours active spells cancels out.<br /> 3-4 Red Hand The spell you casted backfires in a <br /> 5-6 Seeked by the law The universe has put price to your head a paradox spirit has born to teach you a leasson.He doesnt necesarely must want to kill you.<br /> 7-8 Hunted by the law The Universe knows that you have cheated and he is gonna shut you up.You cannot use magic for the next days equal to your Arete/2 <br /> 9 Go to Jail You go to a paradox realm , a new born microverse/dimension only for you where phisics and magic just don\u00b4t work as they should.You should feel important<br /> 10 Sentenced to inexistence The universe doesn\u00b4t like you , so you just cease to be , maybe Nirvana is a form of ascension.<br /> <br /> Of course not using your paradigm raises more the difficulty making more easy to get paradox dices.So to keep paradox at bay you need to be both consensual and respect your paradigm.And as suggested by @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe\">Redwulfe</a></b> you can always bleed the paradox of out you character but that damages you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T00:13:10-07:00","id":1257509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1257378#post1257378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with the general idea, 5 levels and a fast progression could be a little too tight to compress all the punishment that Paradox represents.<br /> <br /> Vampires can survive a Frenzy and keep playing, Mages sent to a Paradox Realm are, at the very least, out of the story for good. It's all nice and good to say that Paradox should be punishing, but making it's upper echelons as frequent or nearly so as Vampire frenzy it's overkill.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think mages sent to a paradox realm should be out of the story for good. Indeed, going to a paradox realm could be a good basis for a Mage story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T06:22:01-07:00","id":1257556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1257509#post1257509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think mages sent to a paradox realm should be out of the story for good. Indeed, going to a paradox realm could be a good basis for a Mage story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem it's that it will cause a collision of stories.<br /> <br /> Much like dying, Paradox will happen by chance in the middle of an ongoing story. Mage is so versatile that even dying can be the basis for a story - with the live players trying to find a powerful mage willing to resurrect their pal while he tries to survive the underworld.<br /> <br /> But you can't go and explore the story of the character trapped in the realm if you're still trying to save the world (or whatever important stuff you were doing...) in the actual story you were narrating a dice roll ago...hence the player it's effectively out of the story until you can dedicate time to narrate his daring rescue/escape","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T12:24:58-07:00","id":1257627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1257556#post1257556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem it's that it will cause a collision of stories.<br /> <br /> Much like dying, Paradox will happen by chance in the middle of an ongoing story. Mage is so versatile that even dying can be the basis for a story - with the live players trying to find a powerful mage willing to resurrect their pal while he tries to survive the underworld.<br /> <br /> But you can't go and explore the story of the character trapped in the realm if you're still trying to save the world (or whatever important stuff you were doing...) in the actual story you were narrating a dice roll ago...hence the player it's effectively out of the story until you can dedicate time to narrate his daring rescue/escape</div> </div> </div> </div>This depends, to a degree on the preperation of the ST for such eventuality, as well as how story driven the original tale would be. If the game is more player driven, and the ST is prepared for such an event occurring, it could be very memorable as a scenario.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T00:44:57-07:00","id":1258684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1257556#post1257556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can't go and explore the story of the character trapped in the realm if you're still trying to save the world (or whatever important stuff you were doing...) in the actual story you were narrating a dice roll ago...hence the player it's effectively out of the story until you can dedicate time to narrate his daring rescue/escape</div> </div> </div> </div>You could make it so that when the Mage is pulled into or kidnapped into a Paradox Realm, then after an amount of time has passed the Mage is released even if she or he doesn't escape ( through her or his efforts ) , resolve it, or get rescued. However this makes it so that, in due time, she or he will get pulled into or kidnapped into the Paradox Realm again. Possibly with some changes happening to how the Paradox Realm functions with each time this happens. Each of the stays could be as short as a few hours or a few days. The only ways for the Mage to stop being periodically trapped in the Paradox Realm is leaving it through her or his own efforts, getting rescued by other persons while being trapped, or somehow resolving it ( which could be done while being outside the Paradox Realm ) .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-03-2018, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T06:33:21-07:00","id":1258723,"title":"","content":"I think that doesn't adress the problem here.<br /> <br /> We're comparing the upper echelons of Paradox (that include realms, god-like spirits getting angry with you, and nearly unavoidable death) with V5 Frenzy.<br /> <br /> My argument it's that they don't compare because the upper echelons of Paradox tend to be far more final and problematic.<br /> <br /> That they're stories unto themselves reinforces this point - Frenzy may be a story seed if it happens at a very bad time (and the player has enough agency to try to avoid these by expending Willpower and feeding regularly), but in most cases Frenzy is a powerful but ultimately short scene of an ongoning story.<br /> <br /> You proposal changes what &quot;being sent to a realm&quot; means, and doing so lowers the finality, but it's still far more bothersome (you don't get unpredictable Frenzy bouts after frenzing once).<br /> <br /> I don't see why changing the concept of Paradox would be necessary to use Paradox Dice. This problem it's simple enough to solve by making these upper echelons easier to avoid trough player agency than Vampire Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-03-2018, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T10:56:15-07:00","id":1258753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1258723#post1258723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that doesn't adress the problem here.<br /> <br /> We're comparing the upper echelons of Paradox (that include realms, god-like spirits getting angry with you, and nearly unavoidable death) with V5 Frenzy.<br /> <br /> My argument it's that they don't compare because the upper echelons of Paradox tend to be far more final and problematic.<br /> <br /> That they're stories unto themselves reinforces this point - Frenzy may be a story seed if it happens at a very bad time (and the player has enough agency to try to avoid these by expending Willpower and feeding regularly), but in most cases Frenzy is a powerful but ultimately short scene of an ongoning story.<br /> <br /> You proposal changes what &quot;being sent to a realm&quot; means, and doing so lowers the finality, but it's still far more bothersome (you don't get unpredictable Frenzy bouts after frenzing once).<br /> <br /> I don't see why changing the concept of Paradox would be necessary to use Paradox Dice. This problem it's simple enough to solve by making these upper echelons easier to avoid trough player agency than Vampire Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>But at the same time don't you think a mages power is more significant as well? I don't see the risk being equally significant being a problem. &quot;phenomenal cosmic power, itty bitty living space.&quot; The line must be toed harder as your power level is much higher in what you can do. This means that you don't have as much room for error and I am cool with it so long as the ability to reduce paradox is present, through Paradigm, Bleeding, meditation, Tass, or whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T11:34:23-07:00","id":1258759,"title":"","content":"Perhaps they are, but not in a fashion that can be solved by heavy handed aplications of Paradox. Solving that unbalance requires a more careful examination of how magick works. Among other things, you gain nothing by punishing quick cast even more.<br /> <br /> I've debated in VS threads long enough to know that with mages the difference in &quot;power level&quot; it's very relative (being a game that requires substantial ST fiat) and even with a lenient ST mages often requires a lot time and resources to compete with the other splats.<br /> <br /> Unprepared mages can't do a whole lot against a vampire. That's why they do so poorly in white rooms. Mages are perhaps among the weakests supernaturals out there as long as they depend on their skill to quick cast...It's well prepared mages the ones that can pull an almost unsurmountable leverage that crushes werewolves and elder vampires. And it's also these the ones that probably will have their Paradox reserve &quot;well feed&quot;, increasing the disparity.<br /> <br /> Magick should be risky, by all means, and Paradox Dice are a good oportunity to hit that nail, but this risk shouldn't make mages weak nor squishier than they already are as consequence.<br /> <br /> Being sent to a Paradox Realm or erased from reality shouldn't be something that can happen because you forgot your bead and had to put a fight, but rather as a consequence of acts of great Hubris. Preferably as a consequence of lengthy rituals (that happen to be the gereatest power source mages have, the one that trully puts them above all others). And it has every right to be a story of it's own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-03-2018, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T21:02:13-07:00","id":1259174,"title":"","content":"I'm not really a fan of making the Cauls something easier to do, as mentioned earlier in the thread. It doesn't really make sense to me as something that one's Avatar would steer one toward, given that the process is supposed to actually invert the Mage's Avatar. I feel like the Nephandi should be treated as something that fundamentally perverts both Mage and Avatar, in a way that can't just happen accidentally.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see more of an exploration of the way power can corrupt outside of the Nephandi. I think there are seeds of that in the game already: the way that both of the more human factions, the Traditions and the Technocracy, are their own worst enemies. The way the Traditions have alienated the Disparates. The fall of the Janissaries and House Helekar. The power plays in Doissetep, and even maybe in the idea that Porthos knew Heylel wasn't guilty but letting everything happen because of his jealousy over Eloine. Heck, even in the way that Mistridge's fall happened as much because of internal Hermetic politics as the Craftmason's rebellion.<br /> <br /> That'd be the corruption that I think the Avatar could cause: the idea that as a Mage becomes more powerful, they become more isolated, selfish and full of hubris that they lose track of higher ideals for their own personal desires and ambitions. The dark side of personal godhood.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'd like to see more of an examination as to why characters like Mark Hallward Gillan went rogue from their Traditions and what that could mean for the player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 10-06-2018, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T13:35:08-07:00","id":1259276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259174#post1259174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see more of an exploration of the way power can corrupt outside of the Nephandi. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by the word ' corrupt ' in the context and meaning that you used it in your post ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-06-2018, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T16:05:20-07:00","id":1259302,"title":"","content":"For M5, I'd hope to explore how the Technocracy declared victory in the Ascension War prematurely. What is the effect of the rise of anti-vaxxers, climate-change deniers, and flat-earthers on the Consensus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T19:44:22-07:00","id":1259336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259276#post1259276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by the word ' corrupt ' in the context and meaning that you used it in your post ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it in the classical sense of the word. The idea that &quot;power corrupts&quot; long predates the idea of the Nephandi. I think a lot of us focus on Nephandi as the be-all and end-all of evil within the setting, but it really isn't. Voormas is the obvious example. But really, you can see it in a lot of places. The Book of Chantries' description of the politics in Doissetep, for example, show us plenty of Mages who are selfish and ambitious and backstabbing among the folks that are supposed to be the settings' protagonists.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Mage is a game of ego. We're playing characters that can rewrite reality who very rarely stop to think &quot;just because I can, does that mean that I should&quot;? And I think that it's very easy for someone who has that power to start thinking that they're the best people to decide how things should be and start mistaking their own individual concerns and ambitious for what is best for all, while screwing over the people who get in their way. I'd love to see that explored more in M5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 10-06-2018, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T02:44:46-07:00","id":1259373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259336#post1259336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it in the classical sense of the word.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what is the classical sense of this word, if I may ask ? Does it mean that a person is selfish and egoistic ; or does it mean a choice and an inclination to go against values and rules established among and by other persons ? Or does it mean something else ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259336#post1259336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that &quot;power corrupts&quot; long predates the idea of the Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that the Nephandi - as a faction of Mages, and as individual Nephandi Mages - are mainly and principally about power in regards to their outlooks, goals, values, perspectives, and attitudes ?<br /> I don't think that they are, at all. Power - and considerations in regards to it, like using it and seeking it - is an important part of who the Nephandi are and what they do, but it is not principal and paramount except to a small extent at most ; especially when compared to other characteristics, priorities, and qualities of the Nephandi Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T09:28:32-07:00","id":1259418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259373#post1259373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what is the classical sense of this word, if I may ask ? Does it mean that a person is selfish and egoistic ; or does it mean a choice and an inclination to go against values and rules established among and by other persons ? Or does it mean something else ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you think that the Nephandi - as a faction of Mages, and as individual Nephandi Mages - are mainly and principally about power in regards to their outlooks, goals, values, perspectives, and attitudes ?<br /> I don't think that they are, at all. Power - and considerations in regards to it, like using it and seeking it - is an important part of who the Nephandi are and what they do, but it is not principal and paramount except to a small extent at most ; especially when compared to other characteristics, priorities, and qualities of the Nephandi Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not sure what you're trying to say here.<br /> <br /> By &quot;corruption&quot; I generally mean the concept by which people who are originally good and have good intention become base, selfish, power-hungry and/or evil. In the context of Mage's setting, I'd specifically focus on the idea of people who are so focused on their individual desires or ambitions that they end up causing harm to their fellows or their cause.<br /> <br /> I would give you as examples: Grimgroth's scheming in Mistridge which weakened them at just the right point for the Craftmasons to take advantage. House Tremere, as presented in the DA Supplement &quot;House Tremere&quot; is both corrupt and monstrous and gives us some pretty good insight into why the Craftmasons would have rebelled. The various schemes in Doissetep which kept the various power players focused on backstabbing each other rather than acting for the good of the Tradition.<br /> <br /> For an example of personal corruption, the best example I can think of isn't from a sourcebook, but rather Malcolm Sheppard's livejournal, namely the idea that Porthos knew that Heylel Taormin wasn't truly evil, but allowed his fate to proceed because of jealousy over Ellone.<br /> <br /> I think the Nephandi are about what the books tell us they're about<b></b>: a descent into entropy and the ultimate unmaking of everything.<br /> <br /> My argument is against the idea presented earlier: that the Cauls should somehow be easier to use or get to without the &quot;help&quot; of actual Nephandi, or that one's Avatar, no matter how corrupt, would lead a mage to a state that's meant to be so completely unnatural that it inverts the Avatar.<br /> <br /> I tend to feel like the setting material occasionally focuses too much on the Nephandi as the be-all and end-all examples of evil. For example, I'm not really a fan of the idea that Nephandi are manipulating the Technocracy or Traditions at the higher levels as presented in Mage 20, because I feel like there are plenty of ways for the Technocracy/Tradition elders to be corrupted by their own power and ideals without ever bringing the Nephandi into it.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of stories we can tell about a Mage being corrupted, by their own base nature or by their Avatars' push for greater enlightenment/power, without diluting the Nephandi's intended purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T12:00:02-07:00","id":1259440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259418#post1259418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument is against the idea presented earlier: that the Cauls should somehow be easier to use or get to without the &quot;help&quot; of actual Nephandi, or that one's Avatar, no matter how corrupt, would lead a mage to a state that's meant to be so completely unnatural that it inverts the Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you should read the idea presented earlier again because you missed the point by a mille.<br /> <br /> The idea was to make Avatar inversion <b>intimate</b>, not easier. That makes it actually harder, not easier, because now you need to think why someone falls.<br /> <br /> The idea was that the mage leads the Avatar to Inversion, not the other way arround. Nephandism it's <b>ONE </b>of the ways (big so you don't interpret it as the only) of falling from the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Path_of_Thorns\" target=\"_blank\">Path of Thorns</a>, isn't it?. &quot;<i>Despair, Pride, Madness and Damnation awaits those mages that sucumb to the Thorns</i>...&quot;. Well, then let's Nephandism be about <b><i>falling</i>, </b>about willingly embracing Damnation, rather than about being sequestered and tortured until you break in a box - and impossible without the right contacts.<br /> <br /> The idea was <i>to make Nephandi corruption be about corruption</i> rather than being another, somewhat direr, iteration of &quot;dude's going to room 101, let's free him before he converts&quot;. Because rescuing someone before she falls should be about redemption, not about trespassing.<br /> <br /> And once again I'm forced to iterate that never was suggested that mages can't be corrupted in other fashions, because, as Muad'Dib says, Nephandi aren't about power - and corruption doesn't need to be about power either. There are many colors of evil, and Nephandi corruption needs to be about burning the world (a generalization, as even there you can split hairs)<br /> <br /> I don't get that &quot;unnatural&quot; argument. You know that there really are people who want to burn the world, do you?. Thanatos has been regarded as a pulsion stronger or as strong as Eros in psychology.<br /> <br /> In other words, the idea was all about how to make Nephandi more compelling and ess cartoonish moustache villan. It also had <i>nothing </i>to do with making them easier to use, nor the sole or main source of corruption.<br /> <br /> You can't make Nephandi easier to use - they're litereraly &quot;shoot on sight&quot; NPC lacking only a red circle under their feet - it doesn't get easier than that. Loosing your soul to Nephandism isn't ever a spiritual risk for PC following the Path of Thorns because you only need to not get sequestered to avoid it, and after being sequestered you need not to break. Falling is more aking to a physical combat than a peril that exists on the road of Ascencion - and there's nothing easier to use than a combat system. I would like Nephandi to be more...problematic...than that, doing justice to the fluff that calls the the Fallen, makes them supreme corrupters and the idea that they're not tied to one or several Paradigms but rather to a state of the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-07-2018, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T17:43:25-07:00","id":1259491,"title":"","content":"I don't believe I did miss the point, Aleph. I just disagree with you. <br /> <br /> I don't agree that the idea as proposed makes the idea of Avatar inversion somehow more intimate. There are of course people who, by nature, want to destroy everything, but I think the Nephandi are supposed to be more than just sadists and nihilists. I don't think Avatar inversion is meant to be something that can happen on its own, no matter how evil the mage. There are very specific things that need to happen, even if the exact process takes different forms.<br /> <br /> Nephandi can be tricky to use properly, but there are some storytellers who are able to use them well, and I'm hoping that the Book of the Fallen will give us even more to work with. But I don't like your ideas for making them &quot;more compelling&quot;. That doesn't make either of us wrong, of course. But my interpretation of the Nephandi is clearly different from yours.<br /> <br /> I'd personally like to see M5 focus more on ways that Mages can become corrupted that don't involve the Nephandi at all. I'd like to see more tools to allow us to tell compelling and intimate stories about personal corruption that don't dilute the specific narrative role of the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T21:58:55-07:00","id":1259528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259491#post1259491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe I did miss the point, Aleph. I just disagree with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You disagree with things I've never said. For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are of course people who, by nature, want to destroy everything, but I think the Nephandi are supposed to be more than just sadists and nihilists. </div> </div> </div>Where did I said that Nephandy were just sadists and/or nihilists? I don't even think that Nephandi have to be either of these things in the first place. Especially not a Nihilist, believing things have to be defiled and destroyed it's not the same as stating things haven't an intrinsic value. A non-sadist Nephandus it's odd, but maybe not everyone <i>enjoys </i>Descension, maybe a Nephandi does what she does without taking pleasure in it.<br /> <br /> I mentioned Thanatos, an universal pulsion that's every bit natural and has little to do with being a sadist or a nihilist and a lot to do with being suicidal or self-destructive. And I <i>never </i>said that a Nephandi shouldn't be &quot;more than just sadists and nihilists&quot;, or limit to human standards in any way.<br /> <br /> And I mentioned that because there was a part of your argument I didn't understand...it has nothing to do with the idea. It isn't the core of the argument you're supposedly disagreeing with<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't agree that the idea as proposed makes the idea of Avatar inversion somehow more intimate...I don't think Avatar inversion is meant to be something that can happen on its own, no matter how evil the mage. There are very specific things that need to happen, even if the exact process takes different forms. </div> </div> </div>That's the thing - <i>it should take different forms, but it doesn't</i>. The fluff of the Path of Thorns says explicitly that Nephandism its a risk on the road to Ascension, a spiritual corruption whose source can take many forms. But it isn't. What you were doing in the Path is irrelevant. It's a very specific item built by evil that makes you evil if you're forced to enter and choose not to die. The exact process of Avatar inversion takes exactly that form and only that form. There's no way to fail at making Avatar inversion more intimate, it would be hard to make it less intimate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-08-2018, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T15:24:58-07:00","id":1259674,"title":"","content":"For the Technocracy, I wish they would introduce the idea that Technocrats are losing the ability to understand their own magic. One of my favorite sayings from physics is that &quot;the universe is under no obligation to make sense to you.&quot; Quantum field theory might be one of most successful theories in human history, but it can only really be understood mathematically, not using common sense.<br /> <br /> In the past, Technocracy super-science has been rather straightforward, even if it's like Blade Runner or Star Trek. What if it becomes so complex that only Archmasters can understand it? Or better, only AIs (or the Incarna that is Computer). What if Technocrats lost control over technology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24699-ebakunin","name":"ebakunin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T17:19:01-07:00","id":1259685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ebakunin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259674#post1259674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Technocracy, I wish they would introduce the idea that Technocrats are losing the ability to understand their own magic. One of my favorite sayings from physics is that &quot;the universe is under no obligation to make sense to you.&quot; Quantum field theory might be one of most successful theories in human history, but it can only really be understood mathematically, not using common sense.<br /> <br /> In the past, Technocracy super-science has been rather straightforward, even if it's like Blade Runner or Star Trek. What if it becomes so complex that only Archmasters can understand it? Or better, only AIs (or the Incarna that is Computer). What if Technocrats lost control over technology?</div> </div> </div> </div>What you describe it's the experience of every non-enligthened scientist on the Technocracy (citizens are handed pieces of hypertech not even the best of them can understand all the time).<br /> <br /> There's also rare stuff that the Technocrats use and can only be understood by Archmages, there's a neat example in the VE Convention book: A defect you can buy for Void Ships it's that the ship uses a core that was built by an Archmage and no ordinary mage understands how it works (so, if it breaks you're in trouble).<br /> <br /> With the Avatar Storm killing Control, probably there's a lot of future-tech made by Archmasters that no living Technocrat can understand.<br /> <br /> It would be natural for the Technocracy to have stuff that they can use but can't produce. I would love to play a campaign where Technocrats recover a piece of Archmasters-level technology that's so complex and potent that it needs the superhuman intelligence of sentient AI connected with nodes to employ...<br /> <br /> ...but I would also like to see Technocrats being able to produce tech like they always had been - otherwise they wouldn't be mages anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-08-2018, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T00:05:23-07:00","id":1259757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ebakunin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259674#post1259674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the past, Technocracy super-science has been rather straightforward, even if it's like Blade Runner or Star Trek. What if it becomes so complex that only Archmasters can understand it? Or better, only AIs (or the Incarna that is Computer). What if Technocrats lost control over technology?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259685#post1259685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you describe it's the experience of every non-enligthened scientist on the Technocracy (citizens are handed pieces of hypertech not even the best of them can understand all the time).<br /> <br /> There's also rare stuff that the Technocrats use and can only be understood by Archmages, there's a neat example in the VE Convention book: A defect you can buy for Void Ships it's that the ship uses a core that was built by an Archmage and no ordinary mage understands how it works (so, if it breaks you're in trouble).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been pondering a campaign setting (Or heck, theoretically even the wishful concept of WoD gamelines) that deals with a situation that would *perfectly* fit this; A Fallout / Mad Max / TriGun / Last Of Us / etc-esque time in the WoD that plays after a global apocalypse. Whatever that apocalypse might have taken form as.<br /> <br /> Warning: Long post ahead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Was it mundane war? Was it the Wyrm? A magickal accident, triggered by hubris? Nephandi? Did the Ratkin unleash the mother of plagues as a radical measure? Was the Wyrm somehow *beaten* and did Gaia, with the triat restored, decide to reset some things through natural desasters? Is everything a wasteland, or is everything being reclaimed by nature? A mix?<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's in the far enough future that people don't even quite remember and history meets fable in the minds of the surviving people. No matter what the origins are, mankind is back to smaller size.<br /> And as we are biologically prone to, we are back to more tribal communities and havens. People struggle and survive, some communities had early access to more technology and knowledge, some less so. But in general, things are pre-industrial-revolution as the means to mass-produce simply are gone, and some places are downright medieval.<br /> <br /> What does this mean for the supernaturals?<br /> Ignoring different effects depending on the nature of the apocalypse, it's clear that certain structures of the supernatural world also crumbled. large sects and groups crumbled or fractured. It's a time of schisms. And ,mirroring human society, more tribalism. Vampires are back to a more feudal state. 'Low' clans handled the apocalypse way easier than those used to luxuries and power. The Garou Nation, with the common big enemy having lost (or won), lost its reason d'etre and has broken up. Human communities are protected by certain gifted individuals able to deal with danger more than others (Hunters).<br /> <br /> And in general, as with human tribes and more separation due to lack of any long-distance communication goes, 'superstition', tribal habits and unique cultures form.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where does this leave the mages?<br /> Well. All it took was, in a twist of irony, the downfall of humanity to put the Traditions and the Technocracy on somewhat even ground once more.<br /> With the rise of belief in something other than technology, mysticism and shamanic culture is growing once more, mixed with the remnants of old technology still understood.<br /> The Technocracy, hit hardest due to the apocalypse happening during the Avatar Storm, lost an incredibly vast amount of knowledge. Not just Masters, but many high-profile mages are long gone in generations past.<br /> <br /> But the Technocracy does what it does best; It stays in the shadows, organizes in Fallout-Institute-like structures, and tries to protect humanity. With even the last obvious remnants of Control and the old higher-ups gone, the union has regrouped into units that are more shrouded in folklore mystery than even during their hayday of late 1900's conspiracies.<br /> <br /> However, with the loss of that vast amount of knowledge come attempts at understanding the height of Technocratic hypertech again - and a concentrated effort of pulling it away from normal society as much as possible. Mundane wandering nomads find strange old bunkers with 'Golden Age' technology that seems absolutely impossible to even comprehend, and strange sites of impossible materials become tales of legend. And often enough, traders in these ancient collections cross lines with strange people wielding even stranger weapony and cloth, seemingly hellbent on relieving them of those goods in a peaceful or hostile manner before disappearing again..<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the lines of hostility or cooperation between the Traditions and Technocracy blur, depending on where you go. Open (or subtle) conflict in some areas meets subtle cooperation for the betterment of living in other communities. The Union perhaps even has become Union(s) where the &quot;partylines&quot; are at odds. And of course there are always renegades, establishing their own little territories..<br /> <br /> And the Umbral landscape? Oh boy.<br /> <br /> -----","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-03-2019, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T09:53:15-07:00","id":1259828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ebakunin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259674#post1259674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Technocracy, I wish they would introduce the idea that Technocrats are losing the ability to understand their own magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another possibility for a problem and an issue within the Technocracy is the Conventions of the Technocracy not understanding at all some parts of the Magick, the methods, and the technology of the other Conventions ; to the point of not being able to use it under any circumstances ( even with precise instructions or tutelage ) , or to cooperate efficiently with Technocrats of other Conventions than the one a given Technocrat is in.<br /> While it is already like this to an extent, in such a scenario the Conventions of the Technocracy would be practically isolated from each other in regards to their Magick, the technologies used by them, and their methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-09-2018, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-13T16:05:40-07:00","id":1260463,"title":"","content":"I would personally change a few minor cosmological details - for one, the Sun would link to the Shard Realm of Prime. But I'm not really interested in grand changes to the setting or mechanics - I'm fine with M20 and am personally a bit worried (liking the Technocracy as a PC faction) that the Technocratic Union will be essentially reverted to what it was in 1e. But this might just be paranoia - I do have something of a nervous disposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 10-13-2018, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T13:42:43-07:00","id":1262721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1260463#post1260463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But I'm not really interested in grand changes to the setting or mechanics - I'm fine with M20 and am personally a bit worried (liking the Technocracy as a PC faction) that the Technocratic Union will be essentially reverted to what it was in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>The M:tA writers could do something more complex than either ignoring the 1st M:tA edition portrayal of the Technocracy, or reverting to it. I think it could be very interesting if it the 1st edition Technocracy, and how Technocrats acted back then, would be made into and defined as a part of the Technocracy that is a distinctly separate and to a large extent independent organization within the Technocracy. ; a group that is a radical and coldly efficient Technocracy within the Technocracy. The one whose members use doublethinking, ruin lives of young Tradition Mages, forcibly draft any encountered young Mages, and monitor the rest of the Technocracy just for the sake of observation and additional data ( and because of other reasons, of course ) ....<br /> This organization is not necessarily bad or unpleasant for every person who encounters it's members and agents ; but ( for example ) those Technocrats don't take a &quot;no&quot; or ignoring them for an answer, at all. Nor do they halt their actions or stop to negotiate without a guarantee and/or a recompense being made for the time and resources they have lost, because they had to alter or abandon a prior course of action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-25-2018, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T16:08:50-07:00","id":1262764,"title":"","content":"Actually, there is one major change I would make - replacing the Quintesence/Paradox wheel with separate tracks for Quintessence and Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T06:14:53-08:00","id":1265260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1259528#post1259528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing - <i>it should take different forms, but it doesn't</i>. The fluff of the Path of Thorns says explicitly that Nephandism its a risk on the road to Ascension, a spiritual corruption whose source can take many forms. But it isn't. What you were doing in the Path is irrelevant. It's a very specific item built by evil that makes you evil if you're forced to enter and choose not to die. The exact process of Avatar inversion takes exactly that form and only that form.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is this part of <i>the Book of Madness</i> 2nd edition that briefly describes a Caul and entering it, which suggests that the Avatar Inversion is done in the same way for each person ; but there is also a contradictory statement in the description of the Malfean Nephandi in the same book, where it says that this group's equivalent of entering the Caul is traversing the Black Spiral.<br /> <br /> I prefer the idea that the Avatar Inversion can be done in various ways, the majority of which involve nothing resembling entering a ' caul ' . I think that if a group would have such a capability like the Avatar Inversion, then they would also be able of making it have many forms. The Avatar Inversion, however it is done, is the initiation into the Nephandi faction. A Nephandi Mage's initiation into one of the Nephandi sub-factions is done separately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-07-2018, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T06:41:09-08:00","id":1265264,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree on that.<br /> <br /> Altrough I would leave the possibility to have mages with the Paradigms of the sub-factions that aren't Nephandi yet. Nephandism isn't a Paradigm nor a Practice, but their sub-sects do have Paradigms/Practices that could be learned by other, non-fallen, mages. Evil and crazy mages could want to worship Lovcraftian entities or the Wyrm for power. Now doing these things does propitiate the fall (if you weren't in a Caul yet, what are you waiting for!), but that's all the more reason to teach the love of Cthulhu to more than just Nephandi<br /> <br /> It was my idea for a house rule that Nephandi, being less easy to manage since now the Cauls aren't a convinient machine you can toss anyone into but a state of the soul, would be like the rock-stars of these sub-factions: Their Inverted Avatars allowing a deeper level of communion with the Dark Lords than what normal cultists can get (regardless of how crazy or evil they may be).<br /> I don't know how that got misunderstood into making Nephandi &quot;relatable&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-07-2018, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T09:23:20-08:00","id":1265294,"title":"","content":"<u><b>What I want</b></u><br /> Personally my dream game of mage would be a mix bewtween awakening and ascension where the supernal , the exarchs and the uber archmages exist.There the reality is stable becuase it will be a reflection of the supernal but consensus would still be a thing becuase it will limit the magic of the non-archmages thanks to the paradox.<br /> <br /> Normal Mages even Masters won\u00b4t know anything about the supernal and in a similar sense to ascension they will be fighting over the consensus becuase of hubris.(The wonderful technocrazy vs the traditions conflict will stay).The reason for avatars wanting the mages to ascend is becuase they will be fallen supernal beings/symbols wanting them to become archmages to fight the exarchs.<br /> <br /> That said I feel that this is something difficult to happen in this sad consensual reality unless they reworked the archmages into the interesting cosmic beings they are in mage the awakening thaks to a new M5 Masters of the Art suplement while leaving to the core have the classic stuff .Just Think about it NWW , OPP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>What I want and is posible</b></u><br /> <br /> I want the technocracy conventions being playable along all the nine traditions in the core<br /> <br /> A non restrictible mechanic system that allows you to play however you want.Don\u00b4t design the system to be something limitating that forces me to play street level campaigns.I want to be free to explore the world in search of enlighment.<br /> <br /> The avatar storm gone old masters are returning , how will the young aprentices from the traditions and technocracy that have taken control of thing in earth will react to this.This is the good way of going back to the 90s<br /> <br /> Technocracy civil war , the Order of Reason vs The Nephandi faction of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Let\u00b4s center in to ascension , the consensus war would be still a thing but I also want stories about the search of enlightment and mages being too much curious for their own sake<br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <u><b>What I don\u00b4t want</b></u><br /> <br /> A street restrictive system of rules , this is one of the main reasons why I and other people don\u00b4t like V5<br /> <br /> Not using the going back to the origins excuse to cut content from the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T09:40:20-08:00","id":1265299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1265294#post1265294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>What I don\u00b4t want</b></u><br /> <br /> A street restrictive system of rules , this is one of the main reasons why I and other people don\u00b4t like V5</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen.<br /> <br /> That was what I disliked the most about Revised and the main reason my group never upgraded Second Edition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T12:40:40-08:00","id":1266474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1265264#post1265264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I agree on that.<br /> <br /> Altrough I would leave the possibility to have mages with the Paradigms of the sub-factions that aren't Nephandi yet. Nephandism isn't a Paradigm nor a Practice, but their sub-sects do have Paradigms/Practices that could be learned by other, non-fallen, mages. Evil and crazy mages could want to worship Lovcraftian entities or the Wyrm for power. Now doing these things does propitiate the fall (if you weren't in a Caul yet, what are you waiting for!), but that's all the more reason to teach the love of Cthulhu to more than just Nephandi<br /> <br /> It was my idea for a house rule that Nephandi, being less easy to manage since now the Cauls aren't a convinient machine you can toss anyone into but a state of the soul, would be like the rock-stars of these sub-factions: Their Inverted Avatars allowing a deeper level of communion with the Dark Lords than what normal cultists can get (regardless of how crazy or evil they may be).<br /> I don't know how that got misunderstood into making Nephandi &quot;relatable&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that following Nephandism is, at least partly, a Paradigm and a Practice, as it influences a Nephandus to a significant extent.<br /> <br /> What you wrote about those Mages who aren't Nephandi is an intriguing idea, but I prefer for it to be otherwise. I don't think that such Mages would be following Paradigms of the Nephandi sub-factions - from what I understand, the Nephandi of the sub-factions have a distinctly and definitely Nephandic bent to their sub-faction derived ideas and actions.<br /> Mages who have a Paradigm and Practice based on the infernal, or the Wyrm, or the lovecraftian etc. , and who aren't Nephandi , are an intriguing idea ; one that I think could be explored, defined, and described in M:tA in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-13-2018, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T13:03:44-08:00","id":1266481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1265294#post1265294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>What I want</b></u><br /> Personally my dream game of mage would be a mix bewtween awakening and ascension where the supernal , the exarchs and the uber archmages exist.There the reality is stable becuase it will be a reflection of the supernal but consensus would still be a thing becuase it will limit the magic of the non-archmages thanks to the paradox.<br /> <br /> Normal Mages even Masters won\u00b4t know anything about the supernal and in a similar sense to ascension they will be fighting over the consensus becuase of hubris.(The wonderful technocrazy vs the traditions conflict will stay).The reason for avatars wanting the mages to ascend is becuase they will be fallen supernal beings/symbols wanting them to become archmages to fight the exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Awakening's mythology, with its Exarchs, Supernal World, Abyss, and Atlantis story belongs in Awakening. It doesn't fit into Ascension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want the technocracy conventions being playable along all the nine traditions in the core </div> </div> </div>Would be neat, and wouldn't eat into wordcount that much because Enlightened Scientists are mechanically identical to Mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A non restrictible mechanic system that allows you to play however you want.Don\u00b4t design the system to be something limitating that forces me to play street level campaigns.I want to be free to explore the world in search of enlighment. </div> </div> </div>Yeah - some of the gonzo 2e era stuff returning would be nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The avatar storm gone old masters are returning , how will the young aprentices from the traditions and technocracy that have taken control of thing in earth will react to this.This is the good way of going back to the 90s </div> </div> </div>Yes - Threat Null is a good way to have the 1e Technocracy as villains while keeping the Revised-era Technocracy playable.Disembodied Mages would also be useful as a general threat to all, slotting into the &quot;Stasis-fallen&quot; slot where the Technocracy used to be and a general warning against Paradigmic extremism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technocracy civil war , the Order of Reason vs The Nephandi faction of the Technocracy. </div> </div> </div>IMO Technephandi are kinda redundant with Threat Null hanging over the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A street restrictive system of rules , this is one of the main reasons why I and other people don\u00b4t like V5 </div> </div> </div>Yeah - something like the Tiers system from NWoD would be neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T10:31:30-08:00","id":1266999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1266481#post1266481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Awakening's mythology, with its Exarchs, Supernal World, Abyss, and Atlantis story belongs in Awakening. It doesn't fit into Ascension.<br /> <br /> Yeah - something like the Tiers system from NWoD would be neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can fit as a suplement and would explain a lot of things like the awakening and avatars<br /> <br /> Imagine that the awakening feels random becuase avatars are fallen supernal creatures choosing becuase reasons to fuse with a concrete soul to give them the oportunity to ascend and fight back the exarchs but mages obviusly don\u00b4t know this.<br /> <br /> Imagine that despite the supernal existing and reality being more static the magic is afected by consensus becuase it is being tainted by the abyss instead of being pure supernal true.Due to that mages are fighting for stablishing his own consensus as the dominant becuase by doing that their magic can be more used shaping the normal world in all the aspects not completely defined by the supernal a higher plane that only ascended beings can touch so normal mages belive that reality is full consensual when it is only a 10% but they don\u00b4t know the rest of it.<br /> <br /> Heck supernal cosmology fits in all world of darkness , caine may even be a supernal being dispelled by father from heavens his own tale being a symbol to create the vampires and corrupting humanity in a way it cannot ascend , the same can happen with the demons and lucifer or Gaia , the wyrm and the weaver being weakened supernal gods fallen from heavens and forced to hide in the spirit world , the land of Nod can be easily the shadow reflection of the supernal in other words our world etc...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1266481#post1266481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah - something like the Tiers system from NWoD would be neat</div> </div> </div> </div>Tier 1-3 = Normal mages and Consensus war<br /> <br /> Tier 4 = Archamages and exarchs<br /> <br /> PD:It is posible and it can be done another thing is that I doubt that WW would ever do that but hey I can dream <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 11-13-2018, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T01:28:29-08:00","id":1267222,"title":"","content":"No; as much as I love Awakening \u2014 and I <i>do</i> love it \u2014 keep it out of Ascension. At least, keep it out as The Fundamental Truth of the setting. <br /> <br /> Frankly, Ascension needs to go more agnostic on fundamental truths rather than enshrining more things as such: <i>my</i> preference for M5 would be for it to explicitly present the \u201cReality is subjective and mages alter it through acts of Enlightened Will\u201d as Tradition talking points rather than as The Ultimate Truth: the Traditions wholeheartedly believe it to <i>be</i> the Ultimate Truth; and the way it was presented as such in the earlier editions of the game can mostly be chalked up to the fact that (with the exception of M20) they were all written from the Traditions' perspective. With M5, it should be presented as <i>a possible</i> Ultimate Truth, and even one that has a lot going for it as evidenced by how well it has served the Traditions; but don't present it as <i>the Ultimate Truth</i> anymore; at the very least, let the Technocracy be advocates of a contending view of the nature of Reality that's just as valid as the Traditions' Metaphysics of Magick while being different enough from it that you don't have to classify all Technocrats as either liars or dupes either for knowing the Truth and pretending otherwise or for having the Truth concealed from them. <br /> <br /> <i>Definitely</i> present both the Traditions and the Technocracy in the core book. Also present the Crafts \u2014 though I could do without the budding \u201cDisparate Alliance\u201d. And retire the term \u201cOrphan\u201d as anything other than a derogatory term for independent mages who have either made the choice not to sign up for any of the larger factions or who haven't come to the point where such a decision is even relevant: just refer to them as \u201cIndependents\u201d. Definitely implement something like Chronicles of Darkness' Tiers system, with Independents being the primary focus of first-tier games; Crafts being the primary focus of second-tier games; and Traditions and Conventions being the primary focus of third-tier games. Which is not to say that you can't run a first- or second-tier game featuring the Traditions or a third-tier game featuring Crafts or Independents, etc.; just that the default assumption would be that if you're interested in the tier-one style of game, you're probably going to find Independent protagonists more interesting than members of any factions, and so on. <br /> <br /> Continue using M20's Focus mechanics \u2014 though possibly change the terminology to match earlier editions; while it was a valiant effort, I think Phil has probably lost the battle to redefine terms. So what M20 calls \u201cFocus\u201d should be called \u201cParadigm\u201d; what M20 calls \u201cParadigm\u201d should be called \u201cTheory\u201d; \u201cPractice\u201d can remain the same; and what M20 calls \u201cInstruments\u201d goes back to being called \u201cFoci\u201d. (This last one I say with some chagrin, because I personally prefer \u201cinstruments\u201d; but the consensus appears to disagree.) The main innovation from M20 that gets kept in M5 is the idea that Theory and Practice are presented separately from your chosen faction, just as Foci have always been: as in M20, a practitioner of Weird Science isn't assumed by default to be an Etherite; nor is a practitioner of High Ritual assumed to be a member of the order of Hermes. The converse <i>is</i> true, though: all Syndics practice the Art of Desire, and all Choristers practice Faith. Rather that having an Affinity Sphere, every Tradition, Convention, and Craft (save only for the Hollow Ones) has a Signature Practice. They just don't have any exclusivity with respect to said Practice (either in the sense of them practicing it exclusively or in the sense of them having exclusive access to it). Also replace the current \u201cmystic vs. technomancer\u201d divide with a discussion of internal vs. external paradigms: an internal paradigm is one that embraces the notion that magick is an extension of oneself and emphasizes the transcendence of foci; while an external paradigm is one centered around the notion that something about the <i>world</i> is magical and that magick consists of identifying and harnessing it, and emphasizes the mastery of foci. Mystical paradigms tend to be internal, and technomantic paradigms tend to be external; but exceptions exist on both sides: something akin to <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s view of a Supernal World of Truth that defines the World of Phenomena would be one example of a mystical paradigm that's external; and the Virtual Adepts have an unusually high (for technomancers) number of internalists who view mages as the CPUs of Reality. <br /> <br /> I'd like to see the Technocratic Sphere Variants folded back into the Nine Spheres, for simplicity's sake. Instead of Sphere Variants, allow certain paradigm- and/or faction-specific Merits that let you modify how some of the Spheres work. The Art of Desire should have a Merit that lets you use Prime to treat organized human activity like a Node; the Void Engineers' Signature Practice should allow them to use Spirit to more easily breech or reinforce the Gauntlet at the price of not being as good at summoning, binding, and warding E.D.E.s (their thing is crossing dimensions, not animism), and using distance-based Correspondence ranges instead of Sympathy-based ones (emphasizing the spatial aspects of Correspondence); the \u201cEverything is Data\u201d Theory should allow for a modifier to the Correspondence Sphere that makes it easier to use in relation to the digital world (including the use of something like Data's replacement for Correspondence ranges); \u201cA Mechanistic Universe\u201d might adjust Prime to be better at creating Wonders at the expense of its more \u201cnoumenous\u201d applications being more difficult; and so on. This allows us to tailor the Spheres to individual Paradigms without having to write up entire Sphere variants, greatly cutting back on the word count while keeping the resulting flexibility. Note that this also involves scrapping the Qlippothic Spheres: if Nephandic magick differs from others' magick in terms of what they can do instead of \u201cmerely\u201d what their Paradigm is, it can be handled through a Merit just like anyone else. Heck, even the Marauders' special relationship with Paradox could be handled in this manner. <br /> <br /> Replace M20's three forms of Quiet that are merely an adaptation of MRev's Triat-inspired expansion of Resonance and Quiet with a four-fold set of Quiets representing possible personality pitfalls that a mage needs to be especially wary of: Madness and Denial stay; but instead of Morbidity, you also have Obsession (Morbidity being a particular case, specifically Obsession with Death) and Hubris. These correspond roughly with the Avatar Essences in the same way that the types of Resonance in M20 do: anyone can succumb to Hubris (or Madness, Denial, or Obsession, for that matter) just like anyone can acquire any kind of Resonance based on what actions they take; but the sorts of things Questing Avatars tend to push their mages to do tend to accrue Devotional Resonance and put them at a greater-than-normal risk of Hubris; a Dynamic Avatar frequently fosters activities that lead to Temperamental Resonance and a greater risk of Madness; a Pattern Avatar usually advocates actions that lead to Stabilizing Resonance and a greater risk of Denial; and a Primordial Essence often suggests actions leading to Elemental Resonance and a greater risk of Obsession. Ultimately, the kinds of Resonance and Quiet a mage faces depends on his own actions; but if roleplayed correctly, the mage's Avatar will have at least <i>something</i> to do with what those actions will be. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, Synergy goes away. It was there in M20 mainly as a sop for MRev fans who wanted to keep the Dynamism/Stasis/Entropy triad that that edition pushed into the foreground; for M5, it's an unnecessary complication. M5 shouldn't be defined by the Triat the way the first three editions of the game were; to the extent that there's <i>any</i> overall structure to the metaphysics of the game, it should come from the four-fold Avatar Essences. <br /> <br /> In terms of Metaplot elements, I'm ok with Brucato's \u201cNew Millennium\u201d developments hinted at in M20 to start coming to fruition, for the most part (except for the Disparate Alliance, as I said before; I just don't buy it). Go ahead and start the Technocratic Civil War, with a potentially Technephandi-inspired takeover of Control followed by the exodus of Navalon and the potential birth of a new Order of Reason in opposition to it (with the latter patterned heavily after the Revised Convention Books while the former takes a darker turn). Navalon/the new Order of Reason should be considerably weaker than the Union, but still powerful enough that Backgrounds such as Requisitions remain viable for its members. The Union's traditional enemies should be split on how to react: some want to take advantage of the chaos to tear down both versions of the Technocracy; others want to help the Order of Reason on the theory that the enemy of one's enemy is a potential friend; and still others just want to sit on the sidelines eating popcorn as they watch the former bane of their existence self-destruct (the catch being that shrapnel from an explosion doesn't stop short of \u201cthe sidelines\u201d: I could see the Union restarting the Pogrom, putting <i>everyone</i> in danger). <br /> <br /> This development would mainly be a \u201cTier Three\u201d thing: Tier Two games would tend to take place in locales where the aforementioned Civil War hasn't gone hot, or where one or the other side has achieved a stronghold and doesn't really need to worry about the War; and Tier One games generally don't mess with politics at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T09:50:25-08:00","id":1267601,"title":"","content":"If you have a Technocratic Civil War happen, I think it's at least a possibility for the VAs to join the new OoR - most of their beef with the Technocracy is down to politics. The Batini could then retake the Seat of Correspondence ...<br /> <br /> I would also have the takeover of the upper echelons be masterminded by Threat Null ... the Technocracy's own sins coming back to haunt it is more thematically appropriate IMO than a Nephandic infiltration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T11:59:43-08:00","id":1267642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1267222#post1267222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, Ascension needs to go more agnostic on fundamental truths rather than enshrining more things as such: <i>my</i> preference for M5 would be for it to explicitly present the \u201cReality is subjective and mages alter it through acts of Enlightened Will\u201d as Tradition talking points rather than as The Ultimate Truth: the Traditions wholeheartedly believe it to <i>be</i> the Ultimate Truth; and the way it was presented as such in the earlier editions of the game can mostly be chalked up to the fact that (with the exception of M20) they were all written from the Traditions' perspective. With M5, it should be presented as <i>a possible</i> Ultimate Truth, and even one that has a lot going for it as evidenced by how well it has served the Traditions; but don't present it as <i>the Ultimate Truth</i> anymore; at the very least, let the Technocracy be advocates of a contending view of the nature of Reality that's just as valid as the Traditions' Metaphysics of Magick while being different enough from it that you don't have to classify all Technocrats as either liars or dupes either for knowing the Truth and pretending otherwise or for having the Truth concealed from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the Technocracy's view point(s) should be defined and explored in regard to what they think is true in regard to doing Magick, next to the Traditions' ( and other Mystics' ) perspective(s). It could also be mentioned and described that some Technocrats are aware that the &quot;Perception shapes reality&quot; Metaphysics of Magick appear to be correct to a large extent in regard to doing Magick. But at the same time these Technocrats' attitude is that they should explore the other option that seems a possibility for them - there being underlying trends and laws in reality that a Mage can perceive and work through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1267222#post1267222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Definitely</i> present both the Traditions and the Technocracy in the core book. Also present the Crafts \u2014 though I could do without the budding \u201cDisparate Alliance\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer for Crafts to be presented as self-sufficient ( or nearly self-sufficient ) groups and organizations, without the Disparate Alliance being included ; other than maybe as a recent idea that sometimes comes out in practice when Mages of Crafts interact with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-15-2018, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T19:55:37-08:00","id":1268135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1267222#post1267222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I could see the Union restarting the Pogrom, putting <i>everyone</i> in danger).</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope the pogrom is restarted, more brutal than before (less forcible recruitment, more murdering), because of the Nephandi influence inside the Technocracy. This brutality should play into the potential civil war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T09:41:08-08:00","id":1268303,"title":"","content":"That's what the Panopticon was about in Revised right? I mean, for all the &quot;We won, the Progrom is over&quot; talk that's not what ended up happening anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","user":"History","date":". 11-17-2018, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T14:38:43-08:00","id":1271260,"title":"","content":"Slight change of focus: with the recent V5 fiasco, White Wolf being integrated back into Paradox and shifting its focus back to being an IP manager that contracts others to write books for it, is there a chance that M5 will end up being written by Onyx Path?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T15:51:55-08:00","id":1271302,"title":"","content":"Well, let's see what hints they already gave us.<br /> There's seem to be a narrative building in in the one world of darkness trailer and in the gen con 5th edition conference.<br /> <br /> To quote the Mage part of the trailer &quot;once you came to us for enlightement, but now you have surrendered to the machines.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And while the gen con conference was focused on vampire and a bit of werewolf 5th edition, they indeed gave a hint for mage:<br /> <br /> (to the public) &quot;the first question that we have for you is : If artificial intelligence had progressed as far as it has, that we know of, who runs the technocracy?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> It follow the ITX narrative that was hinted in the others revised convention books (about the iterators amassing massive ammount of data in the digital web and working on the computer 2.0), and in a way, the Theogenesis Gimmick short story of truth beyond paradox.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;\u201cConsensus isn\u2019t yours, Roy,\u201d ExMachine says. \u201c<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t belong to the Technocrats, and it isn\u2019t controlled by the Council, and not by the Nephandi or Marauders either. Your various global guilds and conglomerates try to shape what the masses believe, and you create gods left and right. Gods that are smarter than you. Your pride won\u2019t let you see what\u2019s right in front of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d I interrupt his monologue. \u201cWhat language are you speaking now?<br /> <br /> Keymon translates for me: \u201cBelief makes reality, baby. It\u2019s easier to control beliefs of Sleepers than it is to cast spells. And it\u2019s even easier to control the beliefs of mages.\u201d \u201cI think I get it,\u201d I say. \u201cThe gods handle mages the same way mages handle\u2026 \u2018sleepers.\u2019\u201d&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T09:19:58-08:00","id":1271468,"title":"","content":"I think you can safely ignore what ever was said at GenCon. People making decisions and designing the WoD from now on will be new people with new ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T10:39:30-08:00","id":1271494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1271260#post1271260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight change of focus: with the recent V5 fiasco, White Wolf being integrated back into Paradox and shifting its focus back to being an IP manager that contracts others to write books for it, is there a chance that M5 will end up being written by Onyx Path?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're smart, they'll license M5 to OPP and try as hard as they can to hand the game to Malcolm Sheppard, the game's biggest advocate for the Traditions (and one of the best individual writers on the tradbooks.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T09:35:11-08:00","id":1272002,"title":"","content":"I agree with those who say that the recent V5 debacle will mean a new focus from whatever was being planned. Personally i liked the way that M20 was pointing to an greater focus on nephandi as a significant faction in the ascension war, both in terms of having been a corrupting force in the technocracy and as a separate force. The former point allows for more division within the technocracy and more opportunity to take the unity out of the Union and allow for more factions either breaking away from the Technocracy or fighting to save it from itself. This provides for more nuanced and varied kinds of interactions with the traditions. I also like the idea that Traditions and Technocracy might start realizing that, like the warring families in Game of Thrones, they have been fighting among themselves over who gets to rule reality while ignoring the far more dangerous threats to reality posed by the nephandi and marauders, and that this might again reorient the game to be about a different and more complex ascension war that involves more alliances with people you don't like but need to deal with bigger and more pressing problems. This has been a direction they have been moving since revised and and definitely in M20 but I'd like to see that explored further. <br /> <br /> On another note, with respect to the V5 controversy and its impact on M5 and W5, i would suggest a greater realization &quot;in game&quot; that despite their pretensions otherwise, supernaturals are rarely in the drivers seat on real world events. they may nudge and influence and they may definitely take advantage of awful things being perpetrated by human actors but they are not the driving forces. That seems more real to me and i have never been a big fan of conspiracies, and even less so now considering the real world damage that conspiracy thinking is doing in real world politics. This way avoids the major pitfall (that V5 fell into) of attributing real world and difficult issues to supernatural interference in a way that is problematic for many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T09:59:48-08:00","id":1272008,"title":"","content":"I also would like to see the spheres look a little more like the arcana of awakening in so far as they require less of the combinations of spheres to create effects and can do more things more easily with each sphere separately","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T13:45:43-08:00","id":1272689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1272002#post1272002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally i liked the way that M20 was pointing to an greater focus on nephandi as a significant faction in the ascension war, both in terms of having been a corrupting force in the technocracy and as a separate force. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nephandi have been a significant faction in M:tA since at least 1998 ( if not earlier ) , when Dark Ages &quot;<i>Infernalism: The Path of Screams</i>&quot; got released. The Nephandi's distinct and serious attitude(s) and approach(es) are outlined in the book ; and the Nephandi ranks are described ; and Widderslaintes are mentioned ; and the history of the Nephandi is outlined and detailed. These developments might have happened earlier, in the first &quot;<i>Book of Madness</i>&quot; ( or elsewhere ) , but I haven't read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-03-2018, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T09:30:39-08:00","id":1272979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1272002#post1272002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. The former point allows for more division within the technocracy and more opportunity to take the unity out of the Union and allow for more factions either breaking away from the Technocracy or fighting to save it from itself. This provides for more nuanced and varied kinds of interactions with the traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the &quot;fractured monolith&quot; theme has been overplayed a bit <i>too </i>much in recent times, but the idea of growing tensions between reformists and hardliners within the Technocracy is good - at the same time there should be a similar movement within the Traditions. Maybe a faction that exemplifies the strawman version of the Traditions (as a contrast to the more moderate tech-friendly main group) made up of hardcore 90s-era Ascension Warriors who decided to keep on fighting for their own reasons and youths who heard nostalgic romanticised stories of the 90s who want to live that dream?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also like the idea that Traditions and Technocracy might start realizing that, like the warring families in Game of Thrones, they have been fighting among themselves over who gets to rule reality while ignoring the far more dangerous threats to reality posed by the nephandi and marauders, and that this might again reorient the game to be about a different and more complex ascension war that involves more alliances with people you don't like but need to deal with bigger and more pressing problems. This has been a direction they have been moving since revised and and definitely in M20 but I'd like to see that explored further. </div> </div> </div>Yep, I would like to keep Revised's &quot;cold war&quot; level of conflict over the hot war of 1e and 2e - for one, it gives more things to do with NPCs of the opposing sect than &quot;go beat them up&quot; (of course there should be <i>some</i> low-level direct conflict between Trads and Technos). And of course, the Nephandi and other enemies like Threat Null are looming opponents that can force both sides to team up temporarily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note, with respect to the V5 controversy and its impact on M5 and W5, i would suggest a greater realization &quot;in game&quot; that despite their pretensions otherwise, supernaturals are rarely in the drivers seat on real world events. they may nudge and influence and they may definitely take advantage of awful things being perpetrated by human actors but they are not the driving forces. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how you could do this really, given the abilities of the major organisations. Care to give an example?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T13:57:04-08:00","id":1273144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1271260#post1271260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight change of focus: with the recent V5 fiasco, White Wolf being integrated back into Paradox and shifting its focus back to being an IP manager that contracts others to write books for it, is there a chance that M5 will end up being written by Onyx Path?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope so. I'd hate to see M5 ending up the same way V5 did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T22:11:00-08:00","id":1273205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1273144#post1273144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope so. I'd hate to see M5 ending up the same way V5 did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you referring to the Chechnya problems in the Camarilla book, or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T11:06:05-08:00","id":1273284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1272979#post1272979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the &quot;fractured monolith&quot; theme has been overplayed a bit <i>too </i>much in recent times, but the idea of growing tensions between reformists and hardliners within the Technocracy is good - at the same time there should be a similar movement within the Traditions. Maybe a faction that exemplifies the strawman version of the Traditions (as a contrast to the more moderate tech-friendly main group) made up of hardcore 90s-era Ascension Warriors who decided to keep on fighting for their own reasons and youths who heard nostalgic romanticised stories of the 90s who want to live that dream?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how you could do this really, given the abilities of the major organisations. Care to give an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this theme of fractured monolith has been done a lot but i still like it! But also what i would really like to see is not a fractured monolith but an actual break into two or more factions based on the idea that groups within the Technocracy feel things have gone astray and either leaving to start the &quot;real technocracy&quot; or staying and fighting for the soul of the greater whole. lot like modern political parties or religious denominations.<br /> <br /> As for how to avoid the V5 issue, I think there are certain issues you can say that supernaturals have taken advantage of or nudged in some direction but to say they are orchestrating them is problematic. e.g. You could say that the Holocaust could have been used by the technocracy who took advantage both the war and the Final Solution to move their vision of technology forward, or who saw Nazism as a means of asserting control over sleepers, without denying that the driving causes and driving forces were still horrifically human as they were in real life. Not sure that solves the problem entirely but its a possible start. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12792,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","user":"scifirabbi","date":". 12-07-2018, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T11:56:26-08:00","id":1273291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1273284#post1273284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for how to avoid the V5 issue, I think there are certain issues you can say that supernaturals have taken advantage of or nudged in some direction but to say they are orchestrating them is problematic. e.g. You could say that the Holocaust could have been used by the technocracy who took advantage both the war and the Final Solution to move their vision of technology forward, or who saw Nazism as a means of asserting control over sleepers, without denying that the driving causes and driving forces were still horrifically human as they were in real life. Not sure that solves the problem entirely but its a possible start.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Mage has already avoided this issue - all the factions (save the Euthanatos) supported the Axis to an extent during WW2, but none of them were <i>behind</i> the Axis and in the end both the Traditions and the Technocracy dropped them like a hot potato when they learned the full extent of their atrocities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T12:01:24-08:00","id":1273293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1273205#post1273205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you referring to the Chechnya problems in the Camarilla book, or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>That too.<br /> <br /> However, while, IMo, V5 has many good ideas, the end result is just not for me. While OPP didn't always do things the way I'd have preferred, I have a considerable trust for them coming up with a new edition I'd actually want to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T07:15:41-08:00","id":1281502,"title":"","content":"Though I came into Mage when revised was the present edition, I'm actually bored with the idea of a nicer gentler Technocracy. It's not something novel to me. This always came off to me as the default of the Technocracy, being torn by over zealousness because they're trying to protect the masses and ideological arrogance rooted in them riding European imperalism to bring about their global vision to save humanity from itself. Now, I don't want the 2 dimensional villains of the 1e convention books or the nonsense of the proposed M5 plans, but I did really like how creepy and alien the Union came off as in their basic write up in 1E's core. A Technocracy that is becoming transhumanism gone awry; where the leadership is exploring evolutionary paths that would make them as bizarre as the Maurders and Nephandi, and having younger Technocrats wonder WTH they're really fighting for, would be a lot cooler IMHO. I'd prefer something like that for why the Union has become paranoid control freaks rather than it all being the fault of Nephandi infiltration or the leadership becoming spirit beings, a la Threat Null. The ground work for this was already in place in regards to Control and the Machine controling It-X. <br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 01-18-2019, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T12:25:43-08:00","id":1281547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1281502#post1281502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I came into Mage when revised was the present edition, I'm actually bored with the idea of a nicer gentler Technocracy. It's not something novel to me. This always came off to me as the default of the Technocracy, being torn by over zealousness because they're trying to protect the masses and ideological arrogance rooted in them riding European imperalism to bring about their global vision to save humanity from itself. Now, I don't want the 2 dimensional villains of the 1e convention books or the nonsense of the proposed M5 plans, but I did really like how creepy and alien the Union came off as in their basic write up in 1E's core. A Technocracy that is becoming transhumanism gone awry; where the leadership is exploring evolutionary paths that would make them as bizarre as the Maurders and Nephandi, and having younger Technocrats wonder WTH they're really fighting for, would be a lot cooler IMHO. I'd prefer something like that for why the Union has become paranoid control freaks rather than it all being the fault of Nephandi infiltration or the leadership becoming spirit beings, a la Threat Null. The ground work for this was already in place in regards to Control and the Machine controling It-X.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the serious and very distinct mood of the description of the Technocracy in the 1st Edition's Corebook ; even though at the same time I dislike how outright villainous and/or isolationistic this outline of the Technocracy is.<br /> <br /> From page 33 of the 1st Edition Corebook :<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>(...)<br /> The Technocracy believes that Ascension can only be achieved through absolute control of reality. Society itself must be perfect and unchanging. Order must reign supreme. To create their pefect world, the Technomancer mages are driving humanity into a world without imagination, without hope, without faith. Imagination breeds changes, hope implies imperfection, faith embraces the undefinable. (...)</i> <i>\u201c</i><br /> <br /> About the Syndicate on page 48 :<br /> <br /> \u201c<i>The scariest thing about this Convention is that it is essentially faceless. It obviously exists beyond its gangster puppets and captains of industry, yet no leader has emerged. The real movers and shakers of this Convention are unknown. No Tradition mage has yet been able to ascribe a name or face to the leader(s) of this Convention. Who runs it? Where does he (she or they) reside? How come no one has ever seen him (her, it)? Even the Technomancers' Symposiums have been visited only be representatives of this group. What is the Syndicate's real secret ?</i> \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201c (\u2026) <i>To this day, the Syndicate remains more interested in technology's ability to generate money and maintain power than anything else.</i> \u201c<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think that it should be remembered, for further M:tA developments in regard to the Technocracy, that there are many Technocrats who would consider advancing Enlightened Science to be their primary interest and goal. They should definitely be written about, and elaborated and defined to a greater extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-18-2019, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T13:44:34-08:00","id":1281563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1281547#post1281547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the serious and very distinct mood of the description of the Technocracy in the 1st Edition's Corebook ; even though at the same time I dislike how outright villainous and/or isolationistic this outline of the Technocracy is.<br /> <br /> From page 33 of the 1st Edition Corebook :<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>(...)<br /> The Technocracy believes that Ascension can only be achieved through absolute control of reality. Society itself must be perfect and unchanging. Order must reign supreme. To create their pefect world, the Technomancer mages are driving humanity into a world without imagination, without hope, without faith. Imagination breeds changes, hope implies imperfection, faith embraces the undefinable. (...)</i> <i>\u201c</i><br /> <br /> About the Syndicate on page 48 :<br /> <br /> \u201c<i>The scariest thing about this Convention is that it is essentially faceless. It obviously exists beyond its gangster puppets and captains of industry, yet no leader has emerged. The real movers and shakers of this Convention are unknown. No Tradition mage has yet been able to ascribe a name or face to the leader(s) of this Convention. Who runs it? Where does he (she or they) reside? How come no one has ever seen him (her, it)? Even the Technomancers' Symposiums have been visited only be representatives of this group. What is the Syndicate's real secret ?</i> \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201c (\u2026) <i>To this day, the Syndicate remains more interested in technology's ability to generate money and maintain power than anything else.</i> \u201c<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think that it should be remembered, for further M:tA developments in regard to the Technocracy, that there are many Technocrats who would consider advancing Enlightened Science to be their primary interest and goal. They should definitely be written about, and elaborated and defined to a greater extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I wouldn't want the Technocracy to go back to being predominantly about just keeping power for power sakes. Certainly such Technomancers exist, but I do prefer the more idealistically driven Technomancers that most of us know and love. I would just like a combo of both that lost alieness with this idealism, which can be accomplished by making the Union driven by ideological fanatism. <br /> <br /> I also have no issue with Technomancers more interested in exploring enlightened science. It's just like I said, that I never felt like I had this Evul Technocracy shoved down my throat by the writers, having come to the game in its later years. It's been almost 20 years now since Revised, where they really emphasized a more human Technocracy. However, aside from finding aspects of the older view of the Union cool, the Ascension War should be/have been more than a conflict over if Sleepers reheat their leftovers using a microwave or summoning up a fire elemental to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 01-19-2019, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T10:21:32-08:00","id":1282868,"title":"","content":"My ideal list:<br /> <br /> 1. Twenty years after the fact, the Avatar Storm is finally subsiding. Breaching the Gauntlet is still dangerous if one attempts to cross unprepared or in an RZ unsuited to one's paradigm, but it's no longer nearly fatal to all but the most powerful and accomplished mages.<br /> <br /> 2. Threat Null proves itself highly dangerous in the Umbra, but they stick to their own devices and aren't the existential threat the VE's originally thought they were. Later observation and research confirms they're essentially Stasis' answer to Dynamism's Marauders and Entropy's Nephandi, and at least for the time being they're perfectly happy out in the Deep Umbra codifying and solidifying reality beyond the Far Horizon.<br /> <br /> 3. The Technocracy doesn't self-immolate after all. Cooler heads prevail, and yet another Housecleaning and Reorganization occurs which includes a pretty thorough inquisition and Nephandic purge of the ranks. The powers-that-be don't talk about it (mainly to avoid humiliation), but what's clear to anyone with a brain is Control had been infiltrated which was the source of heightened tensions potentially leading to civil war.<br /> <br /> 4. Instead, the Technocracy changes its core mission and splits into two divisions along the Loyalist/Utopian divide. The core mission, as always, is to create and enforce a global Consensus that trends towards scientific and technological advancement to benefit everyone, but with allowances for cultural and regional reality zones when those values aren't in direct conflict with the Technocratic consensus, and pose no substantial threat to Sleepers. This calls for a shift and lessening of the Pogrom, which becomes a mission to investigate reality deviance on a case-by-case basis, identify whether said deviance represents a threat, and then negate threats when discovered. Utopians' mission is outreach, especially to non-Technocratic mages to establish a state of detente, and to spread the Technocratic baseline; Loyalists' mission is to enforce the Technocratic baseline in reality zones in which it already exists.<br /> <br /> 5. Outwardly, this appears as if the Technocracy really has split into two, with the &quot;good&quot; Technocrats parting ways amicably (for now) and a whole new phase of the Ascension War on the horizon, since the peace will not hold. Really, it's a divide-and-conquer strategy aimed specifically at destroying the Traditions by appealing to its newer and younger mages, who trend towards paradigms friendlier to the Technocracy but also lack the centuries' worth of distrust and hatred. Most shockingly, the ploy <i>works</i>, and younger Tradition mages welcome the opportunity to work with &quot;rogue&quot; Technocrats in an environment where all are free to share knowledge and technique, and benefit humanity in their own ways...<br /> <br /> 6. ...which causes the <i>Traditions</i> to detonate. For older and more conservative Tradition mages, this is unspeakable treason, evidence of Nephandic influence, a sign too much has been conceded to the Technocracy already, and everything else wrong and bad with the world. They're absolutely correct in their summation of Technocratic intent, but the younger, more naive and idealistic, mages can't see it and refuse to listen. Lines must be drawn in the sand, and younger mages have to be saved from themselves lest a new, even more oppressive and dangerous, Technocracy comes to be. Older and conservative Tradition mages congregate, and collectively offer an ultimatum: you're a mystic or a technocrat, no more fence-sitting. And just like that, the Traditions cease to be, because the younger mages and technomagi tell the old farts, whose leadership led them down a path of destruction, stagnation, and oppression for centuries, where to stuff it.<br /> <br /> 7. Meanwhile, the Loyalist/Utopian &quot;split&quot; proved itself simultaneously the Technocracy's biggest success waging the Ascension War, and its biggest fuck-up. A lessened Pogrom means less Conditioning and control over Utopians, and the influx of now-ex Tradition mages means a <i>two-way</i> exchange of information, values, and methods. Utopian Technocrats realize they were pawns in a long-con to destroy the Traditions gone horribly right, and they're already so far off the reservation that were their realizations to be discovered the Loyalists would go after them. Idealistic and naive Tradition mages who jumped ship realize they're now considered enemies of the mystics, and there's no going home again.<br /> <br /> The only way forward is together, especially since these mages realize <i>they</i> were the moderating influence on the excesses of Technocracy and Traditions, and Loyalist and Conservative alike are now free to reinvigorate the Ascension War with a heretofore unexplored ferocity. Thus, the Order of Reason is (informally) reborn, and they find themselves fighting a clandestine two-front war.<br /> <br /> 8. On the mystic side of things, a <i>complete</i> shitshow ensues. The Order of Hermes tears itself apart and dissolves into its constituent Houses, many of which join the rebranded Order of Reason, both of which calling themselves the <i>true</i> Order of Hermes and declaring Wizards' Marches on each other. The Dreamspeakers, who were never very cohesive to begin with, vanish overnight when they disband into regional, cultural, and religious crafts. Verbena and Choristers fare little better, as the groups on the fringes simply walk away. The Akashics, Euthanatoi, and Ecstatics are cohesive enough to remain intact, and the Mercurial Elite manage to pretend they're mystic <i>enough</i> (nobody understands their work anyways) to stick around. The Society of Ether simply says fuck this, and jump ship for the new Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> In the end, the remnants of the Traditions decentralize, eat their big slice of humble pie, and gravitate towards the Disparate Alliance. The DA's don't exactly welcome them, but need prevails and they're willing to cooperate so long as the ex-Tradition mages don't act the damn fool by trying to take over and reform the Tradition Council. Obviously that's <i>going</i> to happen, but for now the Traditionalists are behaving and trying to make allies of old (and new) Crafts as best suits their regional, cultural, and strategic need.<br /> <br /> So, final analysis...<br /> <br /> First, you have the Technocratic Loyalists, who are the Technocracy as always published. Five Conventions, Methodologies within those Conventions, yadda yadda. For now they think the new Order of Reason is on their side, but it's only a matter of time until they discover how far off the reservation they've gone. To them, now that the Traditions have been divided and conquered once and for all, and the RD's capable of reform have been separated from the RT's, the Disparate Alliance is the bigger threat. They're still the biggest, meanest kid in the playground, all the stronger for having purged Nephandic influence from the ranks, but that just means if the balance of power shifts they may cross the Godzilla threshold and look to Threat Null for answers.<br /> <br /> Then, you have the new Order of Reason. They reorganize to accommodate defected Traditionalists, not by paradigm but instead by operational focus and strategic role. Ex-NWO work alongside Quaesitori to ensure operational and informational security, Syndicate enforcers work with Euthanatoi to investigate and bring fraudsters and other criminals to justice, Iterator fire teams accommodate Verbena medics and special forces, and the like. It's uncomfortable, it leads to fuck-ups and friendly fire from time to time and it barely works, but it works, and neo-Order mages realize more and more even if they have different methods and hate each other for those methods, their common ground is wanting to do right by humanity which makes them stronger together than their constituent parts. They just have to survive internal strife and a clandestine two-front war long enough to build a solid foundation for a cohesive whole based on that common ground.<br /> <br /> Last, is the Disparate Alliance. The lessening of the Pogrom and shift of priority to establishing a global Technocratic baseline Consensus, with allowances for regional/cultural variation in reality zones, has given them a <i>lot</i> of freedom to rebuild and grow their paradigms and practices. Together they're smart and experienced enough to know trying to <i>flip</i> reality zones is a bad idea, but on the other hand they no longer have that need. The problem is, the Traditionalists are reeling from younger mages' mass defection to the Order, but fail to see it's led to something truly <i>new</i>.<br /> <br /> At the same time, many resent having to work with the Crafts as equals (perish the thought!), or as part of a decentralized global network of Crafts absent a vertical power structure, and want to reform the Tradition Council. More want payback for centuries of oppression, and want to turn that inch of concession from the Technocracy into a mile. The big question for the Disparates is, now that they have the freedom to practice and seek personal Ascension which is what they <i>said</i> they want the whole time, can they reign in their baser impulses as a sect to follow through or will they kick start a whole new chapter in the Ascension War?<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the one thing I'd <i>love</i> to see is a reformulation of Foundations/Pillars as opposed to Arete/Sphere. I love how freeform the latter system is, but on the other hand it can get <i>really</i> goofy at times, like for example how Akashics <i>need</i> Prime to do anything with chi, despite their being a Mind/Life Tradition and how few if any chi-based Effects actually need Prime mechanically-speaking, or the same phenomenon with Wu Lung and Spirit. And, how easy it is to get lost in the weeds figuring out what sphere level a given Effect may be, and what interplay conjunctional Spheres have with determining Effect level -- like for instance how one can make an area-effect fireball with either Forces 3 or Forces 2/Correspondence 5, or how doing &quot;direct&quot; damage with Entropy is Entropy 4 despite the fact every level before it can be used as part of a damage-dealing attack to some degree. I perhaps wonder if moving to a Foundation/Pillar system, based on minor spheres or somesuch, might be a preferable option for preserving player freedom while mechanically reinforcing the importance of paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T16:41:36-08:00","id":1282923,"title":"","content":"I would prefer the Technocracy to have defeated the Traditions, but for the Technocracy to be riddled with Nephandi corruption - a terminal cancer for the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T20:39:15-08:00","id":1282952,"title":"","content":"Yeah; while I don\u2019t personally like the notion that the Nephandi are the root cause of everything that\u2019s wrong with the Technocracy, I <i>do</i> think that it\u2019s an essential part of the Nephandi to infiltrate and corrupt. Just say that there are signs of corruption in all major organized factions, even the Crafts (who aren\u2019t particularly organized compared to the Traditions and Conventions): only the Marauders seem to be free of Nephandi influence, and that\u2019s hardly a consolation given that they\u2019ve lost their minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T08:28:08-08:00","id":1283055,"title":"","content":"While MtAs is still a WoD game with all the &quot;crapsack world&quot; status that implies, it's still fundamentally different than its sibling games in that it carries what the designers have always deemed an &quot;uplifting&quot; message, which just translates to however shitty WoD is, there's still hope for a better world. That's nothing new to anyone who frequents the forum, but it's important to keep in mind as a framing device for exactly who and what the Nephandi are, and what their narrative role is. That being, the Nephandi cannot and will never <i>win</i>, so to speak; their narrative and thematic role is to keep the sects of MtAs teetering on the knife edge between damnation and salvation, preserve the balance of power by keeping the sects from ever realizing their true, best selves, and thereby indefinitely suspending any forthcoming answer to the key dramatic questions of Mage: is Ascension truly possible, who can achieve it, and what does it mean to Ascend?<br /> <br /> The problem, and the underlying brilliance, to the Nephandi in this is they're a narrative redundancy. The sects are their <i>own</i> worst enemies; the Technocracy wants a world of collective Ascension at the cost of personal freedom, the Traditions want a world of personal Ascension at the cost of collective safety, and all sects are too entrenched in their own belief systems and values to free themselves from their own baggage. The rise and fall of sects is cyclical, each new hegemon falls victim to the same sins of pride and sloth as the one they supplanted, and eventually decays and collapses to the next.<br /> <br /> It's just as easy to forget the transition from Order to Technocracy was a bloodless coup which exploited the Order's failings, that it is to forget the Order itself was born of hegemonic power wielded by the Hermetics and Messianic Voices during the Dark Ages. Meanwhile, the Tradition Council's own inception was one of hegemonic influence and oppression that saw shamanic, pagan, and non-European arts forced to second-class status within the nascent sect, with only the explicit threat of a common foe to maintain the status quo -- and the birth of the Disparate Alliance centuries later being its inevitable conclusion.<br /> <br /> Sure, Nephandi <i>love</i> to infiltrate and subvert other sects to their own ends. To great success, now and then. But, on the other hand is &quot;Nephandic infiltration&quot; the cause of <i>all</i> the sects' woes, or is it one of <i>many </i>convenient excuses for each and every sect to spout in the face of failure to avoid genuine introspection? The greatest comfort for a mage, and their biggest hindrance to Ascension, is their ceaseless capacity for to deluding themselves into believing their own failures were someone <i>else's</i> fault.<br /> <br /> The funny thing about Nephandi, is they only <i>really</i> seem to show up precisely when and where it seems the sects might be on the verge of asking themselves the hard questions about who they are and what they really want, thereby confronting uncomfortable truths about themselves, and actually getting somewhere with this whole &quot;Ascension&quot; thing. Then, in the face of a common enemy, mages are free to set the <i>really</i> hard questions aside until the crisis is over. Of course, none of that matters when individual mages, groups of them, even entire sects, have rivals to demonize, war against, and indefinitely kick that &quot;Ascension&quot; can down the road just a <i>little</i> more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T10:11:47-08:00","id":1283074,"title":"","content":"All true, and in keeping with what I was saying: I'm no fan of the Nephandi being responsible for everyone's failings. I'm just opposed to the other extreme, where they have been successfully purged from the power structures of the major Ascension War factions. In this regard, I like M20's advice to <i>keep everyone guessing</i> as to how bad the Nephandic corruption has become. The Storyteller can make it seem like the Nephandi have utterly subverted Control, while having the truth of the matter be that there rot in Control is primarily of their own doing; or he can present the notion that Control has successfully rooted out all Nephandic infiltrators, only to eventually find out that this was merely a ploy of the Nephandi to lure them into a false sense of security. <br /> <br /> There should be problems in all of the major Ascension War hierarchies; but it should be unclear as to how much of that is Nephandic influence and how much is plain old ordinary hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T06:53:44-08:00","id":1283248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1282868#post1282868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ideal list:<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the one thing I'd <i>love</i> to see is a reformulation of Foundations/Pillars as opposed to Arete/Sphere. I love how freeform the latter system is, but on the other hand it can get <i>really</i> goofy at times, like for example how Akashics <i>need</i> Prime to do anything with chi, despite their being a Mind/Life Tradition and how few if any chi-based Effects actually need Prime mechanically-speaking, or the same phenomenon with Wu Lung and Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Consensus in this forum seems to be to <i>ignore</i> that tidbit of HDYDT. It's trully a BAD rule, and one that's completely marginal to the System as a whole: You can use the Sphere System better if you ignore it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, how easy it is to get lost in the weeds figuring out what sphere level a given Effect may be, and what interplay conjunctional Spheres have with determining Effect level -- like for instance how one can make an area-effect fireball with either Forces 3 or Forces 2/Correspondence 5, or how doing &quot;direct&quot; damage with Entropy is Entropy 4 despite the fact every level before it can be used as part of a damage-dealing attack to some degree. I perhaps wonder if moving to a Foundation/Pillar system, based on minor spheres or somesuch, might be a preferable option for preserving player freedom while mechanically reinforcing the importance of paradigm. </div> </div> </div>Foundation/Pillar System it's great to both reinforce the importance of paradigm and allow great freedom. Visionary even. But it may be even more &quot;wibbly wobbly&quot; than the Sphere System.<br /> <br /> Direct damage and damage dealing it's a problem that you will always have with loosely described powers that can conceivably tap on mundane sources of damage. Even a small breeze could cause damage if it causes something to fall on the head of your enemy. If my memory doesn't fail, nothing in the Pillar system controls this use of magick<br /> <br /> More so, Pillars are even more imprecise with determining what each level allows because the level <i>moves </i> - Pillars, as described in the Grimoire, are specialized and thus can archieve some stuff at lower levels compared with other Pillars, while other stuff would/could require either higher levels or conjunction - and these changes are not allways explicit. This problem it's evident when we enter in areas that *could* be loosely tied to the Pillars, but aren't explicitly treated.<br /> <br /> Like, say, Hermetics and their spirit summoning - something that nobody I know could deduce from the Basic but kinda makes sense once you see it in the Grimoire. How many things like that could be *loosely tied* to the conceptual roots of Hermetic Foudation?, if you start allowing such loose ties you can have everything from teleportation (something that they did in DA canon to Doissetep) to some effects loosely related to Time (that they <i>should </i>be able to do because &quot;Astrology&quot;). If you don't allow these connections then the system it's too limited and wouldn't allow to do stuff that Hermetics are explicitly capable of doing in DA itself.<br /> <br /> Hermetics are a popular example because their Pillars <i>resemble </i>Spheres...and thus people use them <i>wrong</i>. Other Foudations are abstract enough that you don't need to explain that many things could be loosely connected to a Pillar and you <i>should </i>be able to do them, albeit at a stepper cost than with other more focused Pillars.<br /> <br /> This *loose* Domain that includes everything that could be conceptually related to the Pillar or a combination of the building concepts of Pillars it's also found in Spheres, but Spheres are 9 and Pillars are potentially infinite. I'm pretty sure I'm not the only one confused with this aspect of the System<br /> <br /> And the creation of new Pillars and Foundations could be polished too, since it's so important for a System that assumes that different Paradigms could have it's own take on the power.<br /> There seems to be two major philosophies here that need to be adressed: reductionists for whom trying to reduce Paradigms to existing Foundations it's prioritary (which means that everyone and their aunts are Spirit Talkers because Spiritualism it's such a convinient label that can be slaped onto everything midly spiritual - See, Hermetics aren't the only ones doing it) and those who would want to create sets of Pillars for each Paradigm. The former would have folded Vladermen into the Old Faith and would have resisted to give Craftmasons their own Pillar, while the latter would have a different set of Pillars for each Christian sect and heresy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-28-2019, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:29:15-08:00","id":1283345,"title":"","content":"When the V20 supplement about the Black Hand was written, the mages in the Black Hand's employ were given a Foundation and Pillars because the whole thing could be described much more succinctly than attempting to include either Arete and Spheres or Paths of sorcery; I strongly recommend looking at that supplement for an example of how to incorporate Foundation and Pillars into a modern chronicle. That said, it works because a single Foundation and its Pillars is tailored to what amounts to a single practice of magick: when you start expanding to multiple practices, the multiple Foundations and Pillars quickly become the more cumbersome approach. And, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said, much of the simplicity that a single Foundation has comes from a certain ambiguity in what its Pillars can do. <br /> <br /> For M5, I do <i>not</i> want Pillars or Minor Spheres. Heck, I don't even want the Technocratic Sphere variants that the Convention Books gave us and M20 incorporated, nor the Qlippothic Spheres from the various editions of Book of Madness. I <i>do</i> think that makes should be able to tweak what they can do with their Spheres to better reflect their paradigms; but as I said earlier in this thread, I think the best way to do that would be through a series of supernatural Merits that each explicitly spell out one change to how you interact with the Spheres. <br /> <br /> For instance, a Dimensional Science Merit that alters the Gauntlet chart for Spirit to better reflect the notion of other dimensions, and the Correspondence chart to downplay the connections aspect of Correspondence in favor of its \u201cmanipulating space\u201d aspects. An Information Science Merit could replace the Correspondence chart with something more along the lines of the Data chart that was introduced in the Revised NWO Convention Book; and a Hypereconomics Merit could let you use Prime to tap into Primal Ventures and more easily craft Wonders at the cost of not being as good at dealing with Quintessence as a mystical energy source. Likewise with various benefits that individual Traditions were given in earlier editions, like the Order of Hermes' True Names. <br /> <br /> This lets you be more detailed in what the Spheres can and can't do, because you're only one Merit away from making an exception to those rules; and it lets you codify those exceptions about as succinctly as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T16:34:32-08:00","id":1283384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1283248#post1283248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Consensus in this forum seems to be to <i>ignore</i> that tidbit of HDYDT. It's trully a BAD rule, and one that's completely marginal to the System as a whole: You can use the Sphere System better if you ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh believe me, the day I downloaded HDYDT and read that particular turd of an optional rule the very first place on the net I came was here to complain about it. Had me seeing red, that, especially because the damn book was written by the folks who made the game originally, and if anyone they should know better. Don't get me wrong, I see the logic behind it, but the concepts and theories discussed are already baked into the mages' understanding of the paradigm itself, and the spheres, and should be understood as being the basis of tools and practice as opposed to a hard sphere requirement. The entire thing is somewhat ridiculous anyways, because if a mage is going to have those sorts of paradigmatic limitations, there's a 99.999...% chance they have those spheres <i>anyways</i> which makes it no real restriction at all, and simply confounds fluff with mechanics for the sake of doing it.<br /> <br /> I mean, not long ago I played an Etherite whose paradigm was based <i>entirely</i> around Hugh Everett's many-worlds interpretation of quantum mechanics, from which I took inspiration from the M20 sidebars about alternate realities in how to properly build the character. You can be goddamn sure he had Sphere Natural (Entropy), but just because that was his paradigm and because he had Entropy, doesn't mean I needed to add Entropy to a basic-ass DimSci or Correspondence (his other two starting spheres) rote. <i>[Fuck, I loved that character.]</i><br /> <br /> Anyhow, moving on. My ideal for an M5 reformulation for how mages learn and use magic mechanically. Make players name the &quot;Arete&quot; rating in accordance with their paradigm (Arete, Avatar, Dharma, Genius, Enlightenment, Daemon, Divinity, whatever) , ditch the Avatar merit and peg Quintessence caps to this rating, and balance that by pegging Resonance to it. Justify it by saying the mage's own enlightenment doesn't grow, but also their connection to their Avatar and capability to commune with it and channel Quintessence, but that comes at the cost of stronger Resonance (which it does <i>anyways</i> as a degree-of-separation &quot;derived stat&quot; thing). This rating reflects paradigm in a mechanical way by acting as a limitation on what powers they can have...<br /> <br /> ...because we're getting rid of Spheres. <i>Entirely</i>. Put all the powers relegated to the individual spheres in a giant list, as dictated by levels 1-5. Level 1 powers are &quot;Detect Forces&quot;, &quot;Sense Thoughts and Emotions&quot;, &quot;Immediate Spatial Perception&quot;, etc.; level 2 powers are &quot;Time Sight&quot;, &quot;Heal Self&quot;, &quot;Body of Light&quot;, etc.; level 3 powers are &quot;Affect Predictable Patterns&quot;, &quot;Firewalling&quot;, &quot;Pierce Gauntlet&quot;, etc. Players buy the powers a la carte as fits their paradigm (in other words if a character doesn't have a paradigm that justifies &quot;Step Sideways&quot;, for example, they can't buy it). The only exception to all this, is we're getting rid of &quot;Effuse Personal Quintessence&quot;, and making the ability to draw ambient Quintessence and hold more than their Avatar rating, innate to being an Awakened mage.<br /> <br /> Give starting mages six levels' worth of powers at character generation, and make each individual power cost something like 4x level in experience (4, 8, 12, 16, 20). Cheaper than spheres, more variation, and players are in complete control over what their characters can do as best-fits their paradigm. No more players trying desperately to mental gymnastics their way into being able to use discrete Sphere powers <i>they already have</i> that conflict with their paradigm, feeling screwed for having to buy requisite sphere levels just to do <i>one</i> thing conjunctionally (lookin' at you, hanging Effects), or looking cross-eyed at powers within a given Sphere level with little if no utility for that individual character and wondering why <i>that</i> crap cost them 8xCR in experience.<br /> <br /> And, we're killing the Arete cap on power levels. &quot;Forge Psyche&quot; is still going to be a level 5 power, but if a starting mage wants to make a sentient <i>whatever</i> at the cost of being able to do <i>only</i> that, fuck it. Go for it, have fun rolling those 1-3 dice at difficulty 8 until you get your 20 successes or botch out (the more likely outcome). &quot;One of the things druids are most famous for is their mythical ability to control weather, so why is it going to take me half the chronicle to get Arete 4, Forces 4, and Entropy 3, and their specialty sphere's Life so I don't even get a cost reduction!&quot; <i>not any more, motherfucker, tornado away!</i> <br /> <br /> That's just my take on it, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T04:59:49-08:00","id":1283483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1283345#post1283345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For M5, I do <i>not</i> want Pillars or Minor Spheres. Heck, I don't even want the Technocratic Sphere variants that the Convention Books gave us and M20 incorporated, nor the Qlippothic Spheres from the various editions of Book of Madness. I <i>do</i> think that makes should be able to tweak what they can do with their Spheres to better reflect their paradigms; but as I said earlier in this thread, I think the best way to do that would be through a series of supernatural Merits that each explicitly spell out one change to how you interact with the Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think this is the better approach. I'm very much a proponent of the Spheres as mechanics are just gaming abstractions and should be used the same way by everyone at the table. The variant spheres have always been a bit of a tripping hazard to that. I like the idea that Paradigms with an emphasis on computers and modern communication have an easier time with esoteric methods of Correspondence, but it complicates understanding of the rules and leads people to think that different paradigms need different sphere combinations for the same things (which indirectly to the HDYDT approach of adding spheres that do nothing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T08:10:35-08:00","id":1283507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1283483#post1283483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...The variant spheres have always been a bit of a tripping hazard to that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, in my opinion it's not merely the variant spheres in later editions that are the root cause of the problem, it's merely an obvious symptom. The problem is the use of spheres to abstract mechanical growth and granularize powers, and how that conflicts with paradigm and factional fluff. Variant spheres aren't the only tripping hazards, after all -- look, for example, at ongoing &quot;why does Entropy also handle necromancy stuff, but why does necromancy stuff <i>also</i> require Life <i>and</i> Matter?&quot; discussions that were a part of splitting Entropy into Death and Fate in MtAw, and a source of confusion from that action. Or, how Mind is the purview of astral realm and dream-related stuff, which spurs confusion as to what Spirit <i>actually</i> does and what are the <i>real</i> constraints of the sphere.<br /> <br /> If Mind is what you use to go &quot;up&quot; from the Penumbra and Entropy is what you use to go &quot;down&quot;, then Spirit is what you use to go &quot;sideways&quot;, right? Well, how does that compare and contrast to established metaphysics which pegs Horizons to physical spaces, the First Horizon being the edge of the atmosphere and the Far Horizon being the asteroid belt, which implies one can cross the Gauntlet with mere Correspondence? Don't forget DimSci isn't <i>just</i> a paradigmatic variant of Spirit, but rather more a hybridization of Spirit and (conventional) Correspondence to accommodate for those metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Don't even get me started with the Digital Web and how it can be accessed with basically <i>any</i> means. Whether you use Entropy to go down and sneak in via the Haunted Web, Mind to go up and breach via Cyber Realm portals, or Spirit to step sideways and climb the Pattern Web, you can do it. And vice versa, if the mage is so-equipped, but at what point in that process does one cross the Avatar Storm? Hell, the Digital Web is a virtual space comprised of data, which is itself under the Technocratic Consensus expressions of (electrical) Forces -- a mage <i>should</i> be able to achieve immersion absent penalties (or even the need for VR gear) with a Forces/Mind Effect, forget Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this entire post is focused around a single aspect of all possible magic, and how just that <i>one</i> aspect gets quite confusing and frustrating at times. But, frankly, it's the one that always comes to my mind first and foremost, specifically because I had a Dreamspeaker player in my old game who would get <b><i>really</i></b> grouchy about what he could and couldn't do with Spirit, the need for conjunctional Spheres to do even simple tasks when it came to the Umbra but the simultaneous lack of Spheres' full power in the Umbra, and the level of other Spheres' overlap with Spirit which he felt diluted the overall power of the Sphere. Especially when, as he rightly pointed out, once he hit mastery, all the experience he spent to buy spheres for select conjunctional use became redundant. As he put it, he felt more like a Pattern mage who could do stuff in the Umbra, than he did a Spirit mage.<br /> <br /> Don't forget the weirdness that sees Correspondence cover physical space and the navigation thereof, <i>and</i> sympathies, of which a base-level reading implies some connection between the two concepts. What if I, as a player, want to use sympathetic magic but <i>not</i> necessarily have purview over physical space, or vice versa? Or, if my character's paradigm extends to one concept or the other, and the other is harder if not impossible to justify? I'm buying an entire sphere, up to five potentially due to the requirement of Correspondence level being equal to the highest-level of the Effect, <i>just</i> for conjunctional use. Yes, I know sympathetic magic is <i>powerful</i> and there must be some limiting factor on it, but on the other hand the constraints placed upon it by the system are quite excessive, especially considering the baseline requirements in terms of success thresholds, difficulty modifiers, and background work for rituals to employ it <i>also</i> being limiting factors.<br /> <br /> In any case, it's exemplary of why I feel a more paradigmatic, or a la carte, take on powers would be more appropriate to the game system than standardization. No matter how one approaches it, the system's going to be complex and confusing with a pretty significant learning curve for a tabletop RPG, that's just Mage. Allowing players to approach the system in a way they can at least easily contextualize which <i>also</i> maximizes player freedom, I feel, would be preferable to one that's necessarily easier to adjudicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 01-29-2019, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T15:27:36-08:00","id":1283576,"title":"","content":"While I see your point, I think ditching the Spheres entirely would introduce a whole new problem of too many fiddly bits. As an optional rule for those players or gaming groups that are up for it, sure; but as the default approach presented to everyone? I'd rather not. <br /> <br /> Despite my earlier post, I'm not opposed to M5 having something like Minor Spheres or Pillars in it, or even a freeform \u201cno organizing principle at all\u201d system like you're proposing; I just don't think they should be in the core book. They should be an advanced option in a Player's Guide or other supplement for those who are willing to wade through the extra complexity to get the ability to fine-tune their powers to precisely match what they want. But there core book should provide nine well-defined Spheres that let a player design the \u201cwhat can I do with my magick?\u201d aspect in a fairly straightforward manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T15:22:05-08:00","id":1283807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1283576#post1283576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I think ditching the Spheres entirely would introduce a whole new problem of too many fiddly bits. As an optional rule for those players or gaming groups that are up for it, sure; but as the default approach presented to everyone? I'd rather not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree - it would create more problems than it solves and be a major break with how MtA has been handled until now. And yes, the best place to present an alternative is in some additional supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T14:45:33-08:00","id":1284398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1281563#post1281563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I wouldn't want the Technocracy to go back to being predominantly about just keeping power for power sakes. Certainly such Technomancers exist, but I do prefer the more idealistically driven Technomancers that most of us know and love. I would just like a combo of both that lost alieness with this idealism, which can be accomplished by making the Union driven by ideological fanatism.<br /> <br /> I also have no issue with Technomancers more interested in exploring enlightened science. It's just like I said, that I never felt like I had this Evul Technocracy shoved down my throat by the writers, having come to the game in its later years. It's been almost 20 years now since Revised, where they really emphasized a more human Technocracy. However, aside from finding aspects of the older view of the Union cool, the Ascension War should be/have been more than a conflict over if Sleepers reheat their leftovers using a microwave or summoning up a fire elemental to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>A note about the term \u201cmore human\u201d - I don't think \u201cmore human\u201d necessarily means more friendly or cooperative. There are many, many examples of humans acting with general self-interest or pursuit of specific ( or vague ) goal or ideal. Humans can also act in a very hostile, unfriendly, or selfish way. A group being &quot;more human&quot; does not neccesiraly mean that the group would be more humane, to put it simply.<br /> <br /> What other issues and areas of interest you think the Ascension War could be in regard to ? I think the question how to treat mundane humans should definitely be described in more detail. Traditions would like to give mundane humans some amount of respect and even what could be called trust, initiating them into trying to reach greatness in different ways. The Technocracy thinks that mundane humans should be guided without them becoming aware of the various possibilities until \u201cit is time\u201d or \u201cmundane humans are ready\u201d ; and the full extent of many facts and opportunities is likely never to be revealed to them. The Nephandi think that the mundane humans should be exploited, except the ones who make themselves worthy or useful in some way.<br /> <br /> The factions also differ considerably in regard to what they think about Mages of other perspectives and factions, and their approaches and goals in regard to them. These distinction should be described in at least a few pages in one of future M:tA books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T16:00:51-08:00","id":1284411,"title":"","content":"That's a rather one-sided description of the Traditions' and Technocracy's views toward Sleepers. It's also true that many in the Traditions don't give Sleepers any respect or trust; they see them at best as a \u201cbreeding ground\u201d, as it were, for more Awakened, and are more interested in pushing the Consensus in a direction that promotes more Awakenings. Conversely, the Technocracy wants to make the world safe for the Masses, and are trying to make their lives less perilous and more comfortable. And the Nephandi just want to put them out of their misery.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I don't think there's <i>any</i> faction in the War that, as a whole, respects and trusts Sleepers. The closest you get, ironically, is the Syndicate: their Market-driven view is aimed at giving the Masses exactly what they ask for. And even they aren't willing to give the Masses things that they're not ready for (i.e., stuff that's still Vulgar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-02-2019, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T03:33:22-08:00","id":1284475,"title":"","content":"I should have noted that it is a one-sided / simplified description. I meant it as the distinctions with which M:tA writers could start elaborating upon and defining further the attitude of different Mages towards mundane humans. Another one is that the Traditions are elitist, but considerate ; while the Technocracy is inclusive, but harsh. This part of the setting is an excellent opportunity to explore and elaborate upon how much being in a Mage faction influences the Traditions and the Conventions in regard to their attitude, perspectives, methods, and approaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T07:33:29-08:00","id":1293464,"title":"","content":"I feel rethinking the spheres, what they do and how many is critical.<br /> <br /> Entropy, as written, is an Ur-sphere that does things other spheres do. It IMO needs to be deleted. All the fate/destiny manipulation stuff can be rolled into Time with little mechanical adjustment.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ropy-redundant</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Having higher spheres be more difficult to use punishes players. They start off very weak and it takes a very long time (absent a co generous ST) to get a few spheres at 4 or 5. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 03-03-2019, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T10:26:36-08:00","id":1293504,"title":"","content":"I'm not up for deleting Spheres; but I wouldn't mind seeing Entropy reimagined and even renamed \u2014 though I've never been able to come up with a good name for what I'd like to do with it. Basically, my preference would be to expand the Sphere to encompass not just Entropy, but also Dynamism and Stasis in the abstract. Most factions that deal with this Sphere actually don't use it for its Entropic properties, but rather for its Dynamic effects (manipulating chance) or its Static aspects (imposing destinies); of the Traditions, only the Euthanatoi/Chakravanti consider all three parts of the Sphere. And for that, they're treated as if they were somehow fixated on the one spoke of the Wheel that everyone else ignores. <br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> what I'd do with Entropy: it would be the Sphere of fortune, destiny, and doom, something that has been greatly misunderstood and maligned in-universe in the past, and is still struggling under those misrepresentations even today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T12:45:41-08:00","id":1293525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1293504#post1293504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not up for deleting Spheres; but I wouldn't mind seeing Entropy reimagined and even renamed \u2014 though I've never been able to come up with a good name for what I'd like to do with it. Basically, my preference would be to expand the Sphere to encompass not just Entropy, but also Dynamism and Stasis in the abstract. Most factions that deal with this Sphere actually don't use it for its Entropic properties, but rather for its Dynamic effects (manipulating chance) or its Static aspects (imposing destinies); of the Traditions, only the Euthanatoi/Chakravanti consider all three parts of the Sphere. And for that, they're treated as if they were somehow fixated on the one spoke of the Wheel that everyone else ignores.<br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> what I'd do with Entropy: it would be the Sphere of fortune, destiny, and doom, something that has been greatly misunderstood and maligned in-universe in the past, and is still struggling under those misrepresentations even today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy does what other spheres do but better. It does rather little that is mechanically unique, this is bad. The few actually distinct bits should be rolled up with Time or Mind.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T12:56:51-08:00","id":1293532,"title":"","content":"So you said in the previous post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T14:15:47-08:00","id":1293548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1293532#post1293532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you said in the previous post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for the repetition. Maybe there is room for re-imagining Entropy. But from a mechanical POV, it can't be &quot;everything other spheres do but better.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:07:06-08:00","id":1293785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227922-m5?p=1284398#post1284398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A note about the term \u201cmore human\u201d - I don't think \u201cmore human\u201d necessarily means more friendly or cooperative. There are many, many examples of humans acting with general self-interest or pursuit of specific ( or vague ) goal or ideal. Humans can also act in a very hostile, unfriendly, or selfish way. A group being &quot;more human&quot; does not neccesiraly mean that the group would be more humane, to put it simply.<br /> <br /> What other issues and areas of interest you think the Ascension War could be in regard to ? I think the question how to treat mundane humans should definitely be described in more detail. Traditions would like to give mundane humans some amount of respect and even what could be called trust, initiating them into trying to reach greatness in different ways. The Technocracy thinks that mundane humans should be guided without them becoming aware of the various possibilities until \u201cit is time\u201d or \u201cmundane humans are ready\u201d ; and the full extent of many facts and opportunities is likely never to be revealed to them. The Nephandi think that the mundane humans should be exploited, except the ones who make themselves worthy or useful in some way.<br /> <br /> The factions also differ considerably in regard to what they think about Mages of other perspectives and factions, and their approaches and goals in regard to them. These distinction should be described in at least a few pages in one of future M:tA books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I missed this, but I didn't mean more 'humane'. I meant how the Union's membership acts more like humans with motivations and goals, even if they're horrifying for others, and not cartoon caricatures out to do villainy for villainy's sake. Maybe as a Technocrat reaches the upper levels of the enlightenment and becomes some transhuman merger of technology or part of a mass mind or what have you, they could be portrayed as much more alien. Even in that case, the Technocracy is not the 1st edition's Legion of Doom.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}